(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 75, 'one young bull, one ram, one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 76, 'one male goat for a sin offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 77, 'and for the sacrifice of well-being, two oxen, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Pagiel son of Ochran.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 78, 'On the twelfth day Ahira son of Enan, the leader of the Naphtalites:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 79, 'his offering was one silver plate weighing one hundred thirty shekels, one silver basin weighing seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of choice flour mixed with oil for a grain offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 80, 'one golden dish weighing ten shekels, full of incense;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 81, 'one young bull, one ram, one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 82, 'one male goat for a sin offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 83, 'and for the sacrifice of well-being, two oxen, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Ahira son of Enan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 84, 'This was the dedication offering for the altar, at the time when it was anointed, from the leaders of Israel: twelve silver plates, twelve silver basins, twelve golden dishes,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 85, 'each silver plate weighing one hundred thirty shekels and each basin seventy, all the silver of the vessels two thousand four hundred shekels according to the shekel of the sanctuary,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 86, 'the twelve golden dishes, full of incense, weighing ten shekels apiece according to the shekel of the sanctuary, all the gold of the dishes being one hundred twenty shekels;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 87, 'all the livestock for the burnt offering twelve bulls, twelve rams, twelve male lambs a year old, with their grain offering; and twelve male goats for a sin offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 88, 'and all the livestock for the sacrifice of well-being twenty-four bulls, the rams sixty, the male goats sixty, the male lambs a year old sixty. This was the dedication offering for the altar, after it was anointed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 7, 89, 'When Moses went into the tent of meeting to speak with the LORD, he would hear the voice speaking to him from above the mercy seat that was on the ark of the covenant from between the two cherubim; thus it spoke to him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Seven Lamps'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 2, 'Speak to Aaron and say to him: When you set up the lamps, the seven lamps shall give light in front of the lampstand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 3, 'Aaron did so; he set up its lamps to give light in front of the lampstand, as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 4, 'Now this was how the lampstand was made, out of hammered work of gold. From its base to its flowers, it was hammered work; according to the pattern that the LORD had shown Moses, so he made the lampstand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 5, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Consecration and Service of the Levites'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 6, 'Take the Levites from among the Israelites and cleanse them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 7, 'Thus you shall do to them, to cleanse them: sprinkle the water of purification on them, have them shave their whole body with a razor and wash their clothes, and so cleanse themselves.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 8, 'Then let them take a young bull and its grain offering of choice flour mixed with oil, and you shall take another young bull for a sin offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 9, 'You shall bring the Levites before the tent of meeting, and assemble the whole congregation of the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 10, 'When you bring the Levites before the LORD, the Israelites shall lay their hands on the Levites,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 11, 'and Aaron shall present the Levites before the LORD as an elevation offering from the Israelites, that they may do the service of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 12, 'The Levites shall lay their hands on the heads of the bulls, and he shall offer the one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering to the LORD, to make atonement for the Levites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 13, 'Then you shall have the Levites stand before Aaron and his sons, and you shall present them as an elevation offering to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 14, 'Thus you shall separate the Levites from among the other Israelites, and the Levites shall be mine.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 15, 'Thereafter the Levites may go in to do service at the tent of meeting, once you have cleansed them and presented them as an elevation offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 16, 'For they are unreservedly given to me from among the Israelites; I have taken them for myself, in place of all that open the womb, the firstborn of all the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 17, 'For all the firstborn among the Israelites are mine, both human and animal. On the day that I struck down all the firstborn in the land of Egypt I consecrated them for myself,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 18, 'but I have taken the Levites in place of all the firstborn among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 19, 'Moreover, I have given the Levites as a gift to Aaron and his sons from among the Israelites, to do the service for the Israelites at the tent of meeting, and to make atonement for the Israelites, in order that there may be no plague among the Israelites for coming too close to the sanctuary.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 20, 'Moses and Aaron and the whole congregation of the Israelites did with the Levites accordingly; the Israelites did with the Levites just as the LORD had commanded Moses concerning them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 21, 'The Levites purified themselves from sin and washed their clothes; then Aaron presented them as an elevation offering before the LORD, and Aaron made atonement for them to cleanse them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 22, 'Thereafter the Levites went in to do their service in the tent of meeting in attendance on Aaron and his sons. As the LORD had commanded Moses concerning the Levites, so they did with them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 23, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 24, 'This applies to the Levites: from twenty-five years old and upward they shall begin to do duty in the service of the tent of meeting;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 25, 'and from the age of fifty years they shall retire from the duty of the service and serve no more.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 8, 26, 'They may assist their brothers in the tent of meeting in carrying out their duties, but they shall perform no service. Thus you shall do with the Levites in assigning their duties.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the first month of the second year after they had come out of the land of Egypt, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Passover at Sinai'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 2, 'Let the Israelites keep the passover at its appointed time.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 3, 'On the fourteenth day of this month, at twilight, you shall keep it at its appointed time; according to all its statutes and all its regulations you shall keep it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 4, 'So Moses told the Israelites that they should keep the passover.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 5, 'They kept the passover in the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month, at twilight, in the wilderness of Sinai. Just as the LORD had commanded Moses, so the Israelites did.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 6, 'Now there were certain people who were unclean through touching a corpse, so that they could not keep the passover on that day. They came before Moses and Aaron on that day,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 7, 'and said to him, "Although we are unclean through touching a corpse, why must we be kept from presenting the LORD"s offering at its appointed time among the Israelites?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 8, 'Moses spoke to them, "Wait, so that I may hear what the LORD will command concerning you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 9, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 10, 'Speak to the Israelites, saying: Anyone of you or your descendants who is unclean through touching a corpse, or is away on a journey, shall still keep the passover to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 11, 'In the second month on the fourteenth day, at twilight, they shall keep it; they shall eat it with unleavened bread and bitter herbs.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 12, 'They shall leave none of it until morning, nor break a bone of it; according to all the statute for the passover they shall keep it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 13, 'But anyone who is clean and is not on a journey, and yet refrains from keeping the passover, shall be cut off from the people for not presenting the LORD"s offering at its appointed time; such a one shall bear the consequences for the sin.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 14, 'Any alien residing among you who wishes to keep the passover to the LORD shall do so according to the statute of the passover and according to its regulation; you shall have one statute for both the resident alien and the native.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 15, 'On the day the tabernacle was set up, the cloud covered the tabernacle, the tent of the covenant; and from evening until morning it was over the tabernacle, having the appearance of fire.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Cloud and the Fire'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 16, 'It was always so: the cloud covered it by day and the appearance of fire by night.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 17, 'Whenever the cloud lifted from over the tent, then the Israelites would set out; and in the place where the cloud settled down, there the Israelites would camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 18, 'At the command of the LORD the Israelites would set out, and at the command of the LORD they would camp. As long as the cloud rested over the tabernacle, they would remain in camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 19, 'Even when the cloud continued over the tabernacle many days, the Israelites would keep the charge of the LORD, and would not set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 20, 'Sometimes the cloud would remain a few days over the tabernacle, and according to the command of the LORD they would remain in camp; then according to the command of the LORD they would set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 21, 'Sometimes the cloud would remain from evening until morning; and when the cloud lifted in the morning, they would set out, or if it continued for a day and a night, when the cloud lifted they would set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 22, 'Whether it was two days, or a month, or a longer time, that the cloud continued over the tabernacle, resting upon it, the Israelites would remain in camp and would not set out; but when it lifted they would set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 9, 23, 'At the command of the LORD they would camp, and at the command of the LORD they would set out. They kept the charge of the LORD, at the command of the LORD by Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Silver Trumpets'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 2, 'Make two silver trumpets; you shall make them of hammered work; and you shall use them for summoning the congregation, and for breaking camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 3, 'When both are blown, the whole congregation shall assemble before you at the entrance of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 4, 'But if only one is blown, then the leaders, the heads of the tribes of Israel, shall assemble before you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 5, 'When you blow an alarm, the camps on the east side shall set out;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 6, 'when you blow a second alarm, the camps on the south side shall set out. An alarm is to be blown whenever they are to set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 7, 'But when the assembly is to be gathered, you shall blow, but you shall not sound an alarm.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 8, 'The sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow the trumpets; this shall be a perpetual institution for you throughout your generations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 9, 'When you go to war in your land against the adversary who oppresses you, you shall sound an alarm with the trumpets, so that you may be remembered before the LORD your God and be saved from your enemies.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 10, 'Also on your days of rejoicing, at your appointed festivals, and at the beginnings of your months, you shall blow the trumpets over your burnt offerings and over your sacrifices of well-being; they shall serve as a reminder on your behalf before the LORD your God: I am the LORD your God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 11, 'In the second year, in the second month, on the twentieth day of the month, the cloud lifted from over the tabernacle of the covenant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Departure from Sinai'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 12, 'Then the Israelites set out by stages from the wilderness of Sinai, and the cloud settled down in the wilderness of Paran.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 13, 'They set out for the first time at the command of the LORD by Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 14, 'The standard of the camp of Judah set out first, company by company, and over the whole company was Nahshon son of Amminadab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 15, 'Over the company of the tribe of Issachar was Nethanel son of Zuar;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 16, 'and over the company of the tribe of Zebulun was Eliab son of Helon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 17, 'Then the tabernacle was taken down, and the Gershonites and the Merarites, who carried the tabernacle, set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 18, 'Next the standard of the camp of Reuben set out, company by company; and over the whole company was Elizur son of Shedeur.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 19, 'Over the company of the tribe of Simeon was Shelumiel son of Zurishaddai,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 20, 'and over the company of the tribe of Gad was Eliasaph son of Deuel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 21, 'Then the Kohathites, who carried the holy things, set out; and the tabernacle was set up before their arrival.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 22, 'Next the standard of the Ephraimite camp set out, company by company, and over the whole company was Elishama son of Ammihud.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 23, 'Over the company of the tribe of Manasseh was Gamaliel son of Pedahzur,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 24, 'and over the company of the tribe of Benjamin was Abidan son of Gideoni.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 25, 'Then the standard of the camp of Dan, acting as the rear guard of all the camps, set out, company by company, and over the whole company was Ahiezer son of Ammishaddai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 26, 'Over the company of the tribe of Asher was Pagiel son of Ochran,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 27, 'and over the company of the tribe of Naphtali was Ahira son of Enan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 28, 'This was the order of march of the Israelites, company by company, when they set out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 29, 'Moses said to Hobab son of Reuel the Midianite, Moses" father-in-law, "We are setting out for the place of which the LORD said, "I will give it to you"; come with us, and we will treat you well; for the LORD has promised good to Israel."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 30, 'But he said to him, "I will not go, but I will go back to my own land and to my kindred."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 31, 'He said, "Do not leave us, for you know where we should camp in the wilderness, and you will serve as eyes for us.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 32, 'Moreover, if you go with us, whatever good the LORD does for us, the same we will do for you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 33, 'So they set out from the mount of the LORD three days" journey with the ark of the covenant of the LORD going before them three days" journey, to seek out a resting place for them,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 34, 'the cloud of the LORD being over them by day when they set out from the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 35, 'Whenever the ark set out, Moses would say,
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 1, 'Now when the people complained in the hearing of the LORD about their misfortunes, the LORD heard it and his anger was kindled. Then the fire of the LORD burned against them, and consumed some outlying parts of the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Complaining in the Desert'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 2, 'But the people cried out to Moses; and Moses prayed to the LORD, and the fire abated.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 3, 'So that place was called Taberah, because the fire of the LORD burned against them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 4, 'The rabble among them had a strong craving; and the Israelites also wept again, and said, "If only we had meat to eat!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 5, 'We remember the fish we used to eat in Egypt for nothing, the cucumbers, the melons, the leeks, the onions, and the garlic;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 6, 'but now our strength is dried up, and there is nothing at all but this manna to look at."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 7, 'Now the manna was like coriander seed, and its color was like the color of gum resin.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 8, 'The people went around and gathered it, ground it in mills or beat it in mortars, then boiled it in pots and made cakes of it; and the taste of it was like the taste of cakes baked with oil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 9, 'When the dew fell on the camp in the night, the manna would fall with it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 10, 'Moses heard the people weeping throughout their families, all at the entrances of their tents. Then the LORD became very angry, and Moses was displeased.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 11, 'So Moses said to the LORD, "Why have you treated your servant so badly? Why have I not found favor in your sight, that you lay the burden of all this people on me?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 12, 'Did I conceive all this people? Did I give birth to them, that you should say to me, "Carry them in your bosom, as a nurse carries a sucking child, to the land that you promised on oath to their ancestors"?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 13, 'Where am I to get meat to give to all this people? For they come weeping to me and say, "Give us meat to eat!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 14, 'I am not able to carry all this people alone, for they are too heavy for me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 15, 'If this is the way you are going to treat me, put me to death at once--if I have found favor in your sight--and do not let me see my misery."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 16, 'So the LORD said to Moses, "Gather for me seventy of the elders of Israel, whom you know to be the elders of the people and officers over them; bring them to the tent of meeting, and have them take their place there with you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Seventy Elders'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 17, 'I will come down and talk with you there; and I will take some of the spirit that is on you and put it on them; and they shall bear the burden of the people along with you so that you will not bear it all by yourself.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 18, 'And say to the people: Consecrate yourselves for tomorrow, and you shall eat meat; for you have wailed in the hearing of the LORD, saying, "If only we had meat to eat! Surely it was better for us in Egypt." Therefore the LORD will give you meat, and you shall eat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 19, 'You shall eat not only one day, or two days, or five days, or ten days, or twenty days,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 20, 'but for a whole month--until it comes out of your nostrils and becomes loathsome to you--because you have rejected the LORD who is among you, and have wailed before him, saying, "Why did we ever leave Egypt?""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 21, 'But Moses said, "The people I am with number six hundred thousand on foot; and you say, "I will give them meat, that they may eat for a whole month"!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 22, 'Are there enough flocks and herds to slaughter for them? Are there enough fish in the sea to catch for them?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 23, 'The LORD said to Moses, "Is the LORD"s power limited? Now you shall see whether my word will come true for you or not."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 24, 'So Moses went out and told the people the words of the LORD; and he gathered seventy elders of the people, and placed them all around the tent.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 25, 'Then the LORD came down in the cloud and spoke to him, and took some of the spirit that was on him and put it on the seventy elders; and when the spirit rested upon them, they prophesied. But they did not do so again.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 26, 'Two men remained in the camp, one named Eldad, and the other named Medad, and the spirit rested on them; they were among those registered, but they had not gone out to the tent, and so they prophesied in the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 27, 'And a young man ran and told Moses, "Eldad and Medad are prophesying in the camp."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 28, 'And Joshua son of Nun, the assistant of Moses, one of his chosen men, said, "My lord Moses, stop them!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 29, 'But Moses said to him, "Are you jealous for my sake? Would that all the LORD"s people were prophets, and that the LORD would put his spirit on them!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 30, 'And Moses and the elders of Israel returned to the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 31, 'Then a wind went out from the LORD, and it brought quails from the sea and let them fall beside the camp, about a day"s journey on this side and a day"s journey on the other side, all around the camp, about two cubits deep on the ground.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Quails'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 32, 'So the people worked all that day and night and all the next day, gathering the quails; the least anyone gathered was ten homers; and they spread them out for themselves all around the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 33, 'But while the meat was still between their teeth, before it was consumed, the anger of the LORD was kindled against the people, and the LORD struck the people with a very great plague.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 34, 'So that place was called Kibroth-hattaavah, because there they buried the people who had the craving.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 11, 35, 'From Kibroth-hattaavah the people journeyed to Hazeroth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 1, 'While they were at Hazeroth, Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses because of the Cushite woman whom he had married (for he had indeed married a Cushite woman);', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Aaron and Miriam Jealous of Moses'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 2, 'and they said, "Has the LORD spoken only through Moses? Has he not spoken through us also?" And the LORD heard it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 3, 'Now the man Moses was very humble, more so than anyone else on the face of the earth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 4, 'Suddenly the LORD said to Moses, Aaron, and Miriam, "Come out, you three, to the tent of meeting." So the three of them came out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 5, 'Then the LORD came down in a pillar of cloud, and stood at the entrance of the tent, and called Aaron and Miriam; and they both came forward.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 6, 'And he said, "Hear my words:
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 1, 'The LORD said to Moses,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Spies Sent into Canaan'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 2, '"Send men to spy out the land of Canaan, which I am giving to the Israelites; from each of their ancestral tribes you shall send a man, every one a leader among them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 3, 'So Moses sent them from the wilderness of Paran, according to the command of the LORD, all of them leading men among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 4, 'These were their names: From the tribe of Reuben, Shammua son of Zaccur;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 5, 'from the tribe of Simeon, Shaphat son of Hori;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 6, 'from the tribe of Judah, Caleb son of Jephunneh;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 7, 'from the tribe of Issachar, Igal son of Joseph;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 8, 'from the tribe of Ephraim, Hoshea son of Nun;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 9, 'from the tribe of Benjamin, Palti son of Raphu;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 10, 'from the tribe of Zebulun, Gaddiel son of Sodi;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 11, 'from the tribe of Joseph (that is, from the tribe of Manasseh), Gaddi son of Susi;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 12, 'from the tribe of Dan, Ammiel son of Gemalli;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 13, 'from the tribe of Asher, Sethur son of Michael;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 14, 'from the tribe of Naphtali, Nahbi son of Vophsi;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 15, 'from the tribe of Gad, Geuel son of Machi.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 16, 'These were the names of the men whom Moses sent to spy out the land. And Moses changed the name of Hoshea son of Nun to Joshua.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 17, 'Moses sent them to spy out the land of Canaan, and said to them, "Go up there into the Negeb, and go up into the hill country,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 18, 'and see what the land is like, and whether the people who live in it are strong or weak, whether they are few or many,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 19, 'and whether the land they live in is good or bad, and whether the towns that they live in are unwalled or fortified,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 20, 'and whether the land is rich or poor, and whether there are trees in it or not. Be bold, and bring some of the fruit of the land." Now it was the season of the first ripe grapes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 21, 'So they went up and spied out the land from the wilderness of Zin to Rehob, near Lebo-hamath.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 22, 'They went up into the Negeb, and came to Hebron; and Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the Anakites, were there. (Hebron was built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 23, 'And they came to the Wadi Eshcol, and cut down from there a branch with a single cluster of grapes, and they carried it on a pole between two of them. They also brought some pomegranates and figs.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 24, 'That place was called the Wadi Eshcol, because of the cluster that the Israelites cut down from there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 25, 'At the end of forty days they returned from spying out the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Report of the Spies'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 26, 'And they came to Moses and Aaron and to all the congregation of the Israelites in the wilderness of Paran, at Kadesh; they brought back word to them and to all the congregation, and showed them the fruit of the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 27, 'And they told him, "We came to the land to which you sent us; it flows with milk and honey, and this is its fruit.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 28, 'Yet the people who live in the land are strong, and the towns are fortified and very large; and besides, we saw the descendants of Anak there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 29, 'The Amalekites live in the land of the Negeb; the Hittites, the Jebusites, and the Amorites live in the hill country; and the Canaanites live by the sea, and along the Jordan."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 30, 'But Caleb quieted the people before Moses, and said, "Let us go up at once and occupy it, for we are well able to overcome it."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 31, 'Then the men who had gone up with him said, "We are not able to go up against this people, for they are stronger than we."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 32, 'So they brought to the Israelites an unfavorable report of the land that they had spied out, saying, "The land that we have gone through as spies is a land that devours its inhabitants; and all the people that we saw in it are of great size.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 13, 33, 'There we saw the Nephilim (the Anakites come from the Nephilim); and to ourselves we seemed like grasshoppers, and so we seemed to them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 1, 'Then all the congregation raised a loud cry, and the people wept that night.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The People Rebel'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 2, 'And all the Israelites complained against Moses and Aaron; the whole congregation said to them, "Would that we had died in the land of Egypt! Or would that we had died in this wilderness!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 3, 'Why is the LORD bringing us into this land to fall by the sword? Our wives and our little ones will become booty; would it not be better for us to go back to Egypt?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 4, 'So they said to one another, "Let us choose a captain, and go back to Egypt."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 5, 'Then Moses and Aaron fell on their faces before all the assembly of the congregation of the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 6, 'And Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh, who were among those who had spied out the land, tore their clothes', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 7, 'and said to all the congregation of the Israelites, "The land that we went through as spies is an exceedingly good land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 8, 'If the LORD is pleased with us, he will bring us into this land and give it to us, a land that flows with milk and honey.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 9, 'Only, do not rebel against the LORD; and do not fear the people of the land, for they are no more than bread for us; their protection is removed from them, and the LORD is with us; do not fear them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 10, 'But the whole congregation threatened to stone them.
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Various Offerings'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 2, 'Speak to the Israelites and say to them: When you come into the land you are to inhabit, which I am giving you,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 3, 'and you make an offering by fire to the LORD from the herd or from the flock--whether a burnt offering or a sacrifice, to fulfill a vow or as a freewill offering or at your appointed festivals--to make a pleasing odor for the LORD,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 4, 'then whoever presents such an offering to the LORD shall present also a grain offering, one-tenth of an ephah of choice flour, mixed with one-fourth of a hin of oil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 5, 'Moreover, you shall offer one-fourth of a hin of wine as a drink offering with the burnt offering or the sacrifice, for each lamb.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 6, 'For a ram, you shall offer a grain offering, two-tenths of an ephah of choice flour mixed with one-third of a hin of oil;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 7, 'and as a drink offering you shall offer one-third of a hin of wine, a pleasing odor to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 8, 'When you offer a bull as a burnt offering or a sacrifice, to fulfill a vow or as an offering of well-being to the LORD,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 9, 'then you shall present with the bull a grain offering, three-tenths of an ephah of choice flour, mixed with half a hin of oil,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 10, 'and you shall present as a drink offering half a hin of wine, as an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 11, 'Thus it shall be done for each ox or ram, or for each of the male lambs or the kids.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 12, 'According to the number that you offer, so you shall do with each and every one.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 13, 'Every native Israelite shall do these things in this way, in presenting an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 14, 'An alien who lives with you, or who takes up permanent residence among you, and wishes to offer an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD, shall do as you do.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 15, 'As for the assembly, there shall be for both you and the resident alien a single statute, a perpetual statute throughout your generations; you and the alien shall be alike before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 16, 'You and the alien who resides with you shall have the same law and the same ordinance.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 17, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 18, 'Speak to the Israelites and say to them: After you come into the land to which I am bringing you,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 19, 'whenever you eat of the bread of the land, you shall present a donation to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 20, 'From your first batch of dough you shall present a loaf as a donation; you shall present it just as you present a donation from the threshing floor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 21, 'Throughout your generations you shall give to the LORD a donation from the first of your batch of dough.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 22, 'But if you unintentionally fail to observe all these commandments that the LORD has spoken to Moses--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 23, 'everything that the LORD has commanded you by Moses, from the day the LORD gave commandment and thereafter, throughout your generations--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 24, 'then if it was done unintentionally without the knowledge of the congregation, the whole congregation shall offer one young bull for a burnt offering, a pleasing odor to the LORD, together with its grain offering and its drink offering, according to the ordinance, and one male goat for a sin offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 25, 'The priest shall make atonement for all the congregation of the Israelites, and they shall be forgiven; it was unintentional, and they have brought their offering, an offering by fire to the LORD, and their sin offering before the LORD, for their error.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 26, 'All the congregation of the Israelites shall be forgiven, as well as the aliens residing among them, because the whole people was involved in the error.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 27, 'An individual who sins unintentionally shall present a female goat a year old for a sin offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 28, 'And the priest shall make atonement before the LORD for the one who commits an error, when it is unintentional, to make atonement for the person, who then shall be forgiven.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 29, 'For both the native among the Israelites and the alien residing among them--you shall have the same law for anyone who acts in error.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 30, 'But whoever acts high-handedly, whether a native or an alien, affronts the LORD, and shall be cut off from among the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 31, 'Because of having despised the word of the LORD and broken his commandment, such a person shall be utterly cut off and bear the guilt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 32, 'When the Israelites were in the wilderness, they found a man gathering sticks on the sabbath day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Penalty for Violating the Sabbath'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 33, 'Those who found him gathering sticks brought him to Moses, Aaron, and to the whole congregation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 34, 'They put him in custody, because it was not clear what should be done to him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 35, 'Then the LORD said to Moses, "The man shall be put to death; all the congregation shall stone him outside the camp."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 36, 'The whole congregation brought him outside the camp and stoned him to death, just as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 37, 'The LORD said to Moses:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Fringes on Garments'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 38, 'Speak to the Israelites, and tell them to make fringes on the corners of their garments throughout their generations and to put a blue cord on the fringe at each corner.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 39, 'You have the fringe so that, when you see it, you will remember all the commandments of the LORD and do them, and not follow the lust of your own heart and your own eyes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 40, 'So you shall remember and do all my commandments, and you shall be holy to your God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 15, 41, 'I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: I am the LORD your God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 1, 'Now Korah son of Izhar son of Kohath son of Levi, along with Dathan and Abiram sons of Eliab, and On son of Peleth--descendants of Reuben--took', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Revolt of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 2, 'two hundred fifty Israelite men, leaders of the congregation, chosen from the assembly, well-known men, and they confronted Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 3, 'They assembled against Moses and against Aaron, and said to them, "You have gone too far! All the congregation are holy, every one of them, and the LORD is among them. So why then do you exalt yourselves above the assembly of the LORD?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 4, 'When Moses heard it, he fell on his face.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 5, 'Then he said to Korah and all his company, "In the morning the LORD will make known who is his, and who is holy, and who will be allowed to approach him; the one whom he will choose he will allow to approach him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 6, 'Do this: take censers, Korah and all your company,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 7, 'and tomorrow put fire in them, and lay incense on them before the LORD; and the man whom the LORD chooses shall be the holy one. You Levites have gone too far!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 8, 'Then Moses said to Korah, "Hear now, you Levites!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 9, 'Is it too little for you that the God of Israel has separated you from the congregation of Israel, to allow you to approach him in order to perform the duties of the LORD"s tabernacle, and to stand before the congregation and serve them?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 10, 'He has allowed you to approach him, and all your brother Levites with you; yet you seek the priesthood as well!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 11, 'Therefore you and all your company have gathered together against the LORD. What is Aaron that you rail against him?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 12, 'Moses sent for Dathan and Abiram sons of Eliab; but they said, "We will not come!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 13, 'Is it too little that you have brought us up out of a land flowing with milk and honey to kill us in the wilderness, that you must also lord it over us?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 14, 'It is clear you have not brought us into a land flowing with milk and honey, or given us an inheritance of fields and vineyards. Would you put out the eyes of these men? We will not come!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 15, 'Moses was very angry and said to the LORD, "Pay no attention to their offering. I have not taken one donkey from them, and I have not harmed any one of them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 16, 'And Moses said to Korah, "As for you and all your company, be present tomorrow before the LORD, you and they and Aaron;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 17, 'and let each one of you take his censer, and put incense on it, and each one of you present his censer before the LORD, two hundred fifty censers; you also, and Aaron, each his censer."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 18, 'So each man took his censer, and they put fire in the censers and laid incense on them, and they stood at the entrance of the tent of meeting with Moses and Aaron.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 19, 'Then Korah assembled the whole congregation against them at the entrance of the tent of meeting. And the glory of the LORD appeared to the whole congregation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 20, 'Then the LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 21, 'Separate yourselves from this congregation, so that I may consume them in a moment.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 22, 'They fell on their faces, and said, "O God, the God of the spirits of all flesh, shall one person sin and you become angry with the whole congregation?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 23, 'And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 24, 'Say to the congregation: Get away from the dwellings of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 25, 'So Moses got up and went to Dathan and Abiram; the elders of Israel followed him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 26, 'He said to the congregation, "Turn away from the tents of these wicked men, and touch nothing of theirs, or you will be swept away for all their sins."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 27, 'So they got away from the dwellings of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram; and Dathan and Abiram came out and stood at the entrance of their tents, together with their wives, their children, and their little ones.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 28, 'And Moses said, "This is how you shall know that the LORD has sent me to do all these works; it has not been of my own accord:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 29, 'If these people die a natural death, or if a natural fate comes on them, then the LORD has not sent me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 30, 'But if the LORD creates something new, and the ground opens its mouth and swallows them up, with all that belongs to them, and they go down alive into Sheol, then you shall know that these men have despised the LORD."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 31, 'As soon as he finished speaking all these words, the ground under them was split apart.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 32, 'The earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up, along with their households--everyone who belonged to Korah and all their goods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 33, 'So they with all that belonged to them went down alive into Sheol; the earth closed over them, and they perished from the midst of the assembly.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 34, 'All Israel around them fled at their outcry, for they said, "The earth will swallow us too!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 35, 'And fire came out from the LORD and consumed the two hundred fifty men offering the incense.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 36, 'Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 37, 'Tell Eleazar son of Aaron the priest to take the censers out of the blaze; then scatter the fire far and wide.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 38, 'For the censers of these sinners have become holy at the cost of their lives. Make them into hammered plates as a covering for the altar, for they presented them before the LORD and they became holy. Thus they shall be a sign to the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 39, 'So Eleazar the priest took the bronze censers that had been presented by those who were burned; and they were hammered out as a covering for the altar--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 40, 'a reminder to the Israelites that no outsider, who is not of the descendants of Aaron, shall approach to offer incense before the LORD, so as not to become like Korah and his company--just as the LORD had said to him through Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 41, 'On the next day, however, the whole congregation of the Israelites rebelled against Moses and against Aaron, saying, "You have killed the people of the LORD."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 42, 'And when the congregation had assembled against them, Moses and Aaron turned toward the tent of meeting; the cloud had covered it and the glory of the LORD appeared.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 43, 'Then Moses and Aaron came to the front of the tent of meeting,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 44, 'and the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 45, '"Get away from this congregation, so that I may consume them in a moment." And they fell on their faces.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 46, 'Moses said to Aaron, "Take your censer, put fire on it from the altar and lay incense on it, and carry it quickly to the congregation and make atonement for them. For wrath has gone out from the LORD; the plague has begun."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 47, 'So Aaron took it as Moses had ordered, and ran into the middle of the assembly, where the plague had already begun among the people. He put on the incense, and made atonement for the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 48, 'He stood between the dead and the living; and the plague was stopped.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 49, 'Those who died by the plague were fourteen thousand seven hundred, besides those who died in the affair of Korah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 16, 50, 'When the plague was stopped, Aaron returned to Moses at the entrance of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Budding of Aaron"s Rod'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 2, 'Speak to the Israelites, and get twelve staffs from them, one for each ancestral house, from all the leaders of their ancestral houses. Write each man"s name on his staff,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 3, 'and write Aaron"s name on the staff of Levi. For there shall be one staff for the head of each ancestral house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 4, 'Place them in the tent of meeting before the covenant, where I meet with you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 5, 'And the staff of the man whom I choose shall sprout; thus I will put a stop to the complaints of the Israelites that they continually make against you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 6, 'Moses spoke to the Israelites; and all their leaders gave him staffs, one for each leader, according to their ancestral houses, twelve staffs; and the staff of Aaron was among theirs.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 7, 'So Moses placed the staffs before the LORD in the tent of the covenant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 8, 'When Moses went into the tent of the covenant on the next day, the staff of Aaron for the house of Levi had sprouted. It put forth buds, produced blossoms, and bore ripe almonds.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 9, 'Then Moses brought out all the staffs from before the LORD to all the Israelites; and they looked, and each man took his staff.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 10, 'And the LORD said to Moses, "Put back the staff of Aaron before the covenant, to be kept as a warning to rebels, so that you may make an end of their complaints against me, or else they will die."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 11, 'Moses did so; just as the LORD commanded him, so he did.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 12, 'The Israelites said to Moses, "We are perishing; we are lost, all of us are lost!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 17, 13, 'Everyone who approaches the tabernacle of the LORD will die. Are we all to perish?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 1, 'The LORD said to Aaron: You and your sons and your ancestral house with you shall bear responsibility for offenses connected with the sanctuary, while you and your sons alone shall bear responsibility for offenses connected with the priesthood.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Responsibility of Priests and Levites'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 2, 'So bring with you also your brothers of the tribe of Levi, your ancestral tribe, in order that they may be joined to you, and serve you while you and your sons with you are in front of the tent of the covenant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 3, 'They shall perform duties for you and for the whole tent. But they must not approach either the utensils of the sanctuary or the altar, otherwise both they and you will die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 4, 'They are attached to you in order to perform the duties of the tent of meeting, for all the service of the tent; no outsider shall approach you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 5, 'You yourselves shall perform the duties of the sanctuary and the duties of the altar, so that wrath may never again come upon the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 6, 'It is I who now take your brother Levites from among the Israelites; they are now yours as a gift, dedicated to the LORD, to perform the service of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 7, 'But you and your sons with you shall diligently perform your priestly duties in all that concerns the altar and the area behind the curtain. I give your priesthood as a gift; any outsider who approaches shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 8, 'The LORD spoke to Aaron: I have given you charge of the offerings made to me, all the holy gifts of the Israelites; I have given them to you and your sons as a priestly portion due you in perpetuity.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Priests" Portion'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 9, 'This shall be yours from the most holy things, reserved from the fire: every offering of theirs that they render to me as a most holy thing, whether grain offering, sin offering, or guilt offering, shall belong to you and your sons.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 10, 'As a most holy thing you shall eat it; every male may eat it; it shall be holy to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 11, 'This also is yours: I have given to you, together with your sons and daughters, as a perpetual due, whatever is set aside from the gifts of all the elevation offerings of the Israelites; everyone who is clean in your house may eat them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 12, 'All the best of the oil and all the best of the wine and of the grain, the choice produce that they give to the LORD, I have given to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 13, 'The first fruits of all that is in their land, which they bring to the LORD, shall be yours; everyone who is clean in your house may eat of it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 14, 'Every devoted thing in Israel shall be yours.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 15, 'The first issue of the womb of all creatures, human and animal, which is offered to the LORD, shall be yours; but the firstborn of human beings you shall redeem, and the firstborn of unclean animals you shall redeem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 16, 'Their redemption price, reckoned from one month of age, you shall fix at five shekels of silver, according to the shekel of the sanctuary (that is, twenty gerahs).', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 17, 'But the firstborn of a cow, or the firstborn of a sheep, or the firstborn of a goat, you shall not redeem; they are holy. You shall dash their blood on the altar, and shall turn their fat into smoke as an offering by fire for a pleasing odor to the LORD;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 18, 'but their flesh shall be yours, just as the breast that is elevated and as the right thigh are yours.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 19, 'All the holy offerings that the Israelites present to the LORD I have given to you, together with your sons and daughters, as a perpetual due; it is a covenant of salt forever before the LORD for you and your descendants as well.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 20, 'Then the LORD said to Aaron: You shall have no allotment in their land, nor shall you have any share among them; I am your share and your possession among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 21, 'To the Levites I have given every tithe in Israel for a possession in return for the service that they perform, the service in the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 22, 'From now on the Israelites shall no longer approach the tent of meeting, or else they will incur guilt and die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 23, 'But the Levites shall perform the service of the tent of meeting, and they shall bear responsibility for their own offenses; it shall be a perpetual statute throughout your generations. But among the Israelites they shall have no allotment,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 24, 'because I have given to the Levites as their portion the tithe of the Israelites, which they set apart as an offering to the LORD. Therefore I have said of them that they shall have no allotment among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 25, 'Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 26, 'You shall speak to the Levites, saying: When you receive from the Israelites the tithe that I have given you from them for your portion, you shall set apart an offering from it to the LORD, a tithe of the tithe.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 27, 'It shall be reckoned to you as your gift, the same as the grain of the threshing floor and the fullness of the wine press.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 28, 'Thus you also shall set apart an offering to the LORD from all the tithes that you receive from the Israelites; and from them you shall give the LORD"s offering to the priest Aaron.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 29, 'Out of all the gifts to you, you shall set apart every offering due to the LORD; the best of all of them is the part to be consecrated.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 30, 'Say also to them: When you have set apart the best of it, then the rest shall be reckoned to the Levites as produce of the threshing floor, and as produce of the wine press.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 31, 'You may eat it in any place, you and your households; for it is your payment for your service in the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 18, 32, 'You shall incur no guilt by reason of it, when you have offered the best of it. But you shall not profane the holy gifts of the Israelites, on pain of death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Ceremony of the Red Heifer'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 2, 'This is a statute of the law that the LORD has commanded: Tell the Israelites to bring you a red heifer without defect, in which there is no blemish and on which no yoke has been laid.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 3, 'You shall give it to the priest Eleazar, and it shall be taken outside the camp and slaughtered in his presence.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 4, 'The priest Eleazar shall take some of its blood with his finger and sprinkle it seven times towards the front of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 5, 'Then the heifer shall be burned in his sight; its skin, its flesh, and its blood, with its dung, shall be burned.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 6, 'The priest shall take cedarwood, hyssop, and crimson material, and throw them into the fire in which the heifer is burning.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 7, 'Then the priest shall wash his clothes and bathe his body in water, and afterwards he may come into the camp; but the priest shall remain unclean until evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 8, 'The one who burns the heifer shall wash his clothes in water and bathe his body in water; he shall remain unclean until evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 9, 'Then someone who is clean shall gather up the ashes of the heifer, and deposit them outside the camp in a clean place; and they shall be kept for the congregation of the Israelites for the water for cleansing. It is a purification offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 10, 'The one who gathers the ashes of the heifer shall wash his clothes and be unclean until evening.
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 1, 'The Israelites, the whole congregation, came into the wilderness of Zin in the first month, and the people stayed in Kadesh. Miriam died there, and was buried there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Waters of Meribah'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 2, 'Now there was no water for the congregation; so they gathered together against Moses and against Aaron.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 3, 'The people quarreled with Moses and said, "Would that we had died when our kindred died before the LORD!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 4, 'Why have you brought the assembly of the LORD into this wilderness for us and our livestock to die here?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 5, 'Why have you brought us up out of Egypt, to bring us to this wretched place? It is no place for grain, or figs, or vines, or pomegranates; and there is no water to drink."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 6, 'Then Moses and Aaron went away from the assembly to the entrance of the tent of meeting; they fell on their faces, and the glory of the LORD appeared to them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 7, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 8, 'Take the staff, and assemble the congregation, you and your brother Aaron, and command the rock before their eyes to yield its water. Thus you shall bring water out of the rock for them; thus you shall provide drink for the congregation and their livestock.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 9, 'So Moses took the staff from before the LORD, as he had commanded him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 10, 'Moses and Aaron gathered the assembly together before the rock, and he said to them, "Listen, you rebels, shall we bring water for you out of this rock?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 11, 'Then Moses lifted up his hand and struck the rock twice with his staff; water came out abundantly, and the congregation and their livestock drank.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 12, 'But the LORD said to Moses and Aaron, "Because you did not trust in me, to show my holiness before the eyes of the Israelites, therefore you shall not bring this assembly into the land that I have given them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 13, 'These are the waters of Meribah, where the people of Israel quarreled with the LORD, and by which he showed his holiness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 14, 'Moses sent messengers from Kadesh to the king of Edom, "Thus says your brother Israel: You know all the adversity that has befallen us:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Passage through Edom Refused'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 15, 'how our ancestors went down to Egypt, and we lived in Egypt a long time; and the Egyptians oppressed us and our ancestors;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 16, 'and when we cried to the LORD, he heard our voice, and sent an angel and brought us out of Egypt; and here we are in Kadesh, a town on the edge of your territory.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 17, 'Now let us pass through your land. We will not pass through field or vineyard, or drink water from any well; we will go along the King"s Highway, not turning aside to the right hand or to the left until we have passed through your territory."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 18, 'But Edom said to him, "You shall not pass through, or we will come out with the sword against you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 19, 'The Israelites said to him, "We will stay on the highway; and if we drink of your water, we and our livestock, then we will pay for it. It is only a small matter; just let us pass through on foot."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 20, 'But he said, "You shall not pass through." And Edom came out against them with a large force, heavily armed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 21, 'Thus Edom refused to give Israel passage through their territory; so Israel turned away from them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 22, 'They set out from Kadesh, and the Israelites, the whole congregation, came to Mount Hor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Death of Aaron'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 23, 'Then the LORD said to Moses and Aaron at Mount Hor, on the border of the land of Edom,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 24, '"Let Aaron be gathered to his people. For he shall not enter the land that I have given to the Israelites, because you rebelled against my command at the waters of Meribah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 25, 'Take Aaron and his son Eleazar, and bring them up Mount Hor;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 26, 'strip Aaron of his vestments, and put them on his son Eleazar. But Aaron shall be gathered to his people, and shall die there."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 27, 'Moses did as the LORD had commanded; they went up Mount Hor in the sight of the whole congregation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 28, 'Moses stripped Aaron of his vestments, and put them on his son Eleazar; and Aaron died there on the top of the mountain. Moses and Eleazar came down from the mountain.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 20, 29, 'When all the congregation saw that Aaron had died, all the house of Israel mourned for Aaron thirty days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 1, 'When the Canaanite, the king of Arad, who lived in the Negeb, heard that Israel was coming by the way of Atharim, he fought against Israel and took some of them captive.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Bronze Serpent'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 2, 'Then Israel made a vow to the LORD and said, "If you will indeed give this people into our hands, then we will utterly destroy their towns."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 3, 'The LORD listened to the voice of Israel, and handed over the Canaanites; and they utterly destroyed them and their towns; so the place was called Hormah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 4, 'From Mount Hor they set out by the way to the Red Sea, to go around the land of Edom; but the people became impatient on the way.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 5, 'The people spoke against God and against Moses, "Why have you brought us up out of Egypt to die in the wilderness? For there is no food and no water, and we detest this miserable food."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 6, 'Then the LORD sent poisonous serpents among the people, and they bit the people, so that many Israelites died.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 7, 'The people came to Moses and said, "We have sinned by speaking against the LORD and against you; pray to the LORD to take away the serpents from us." So Moses prayed for the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 8, 'And the LORD said to Moses, "Make a poisonous serpent, and set it on a pole; and everyone who is bitten shall look at it and live."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 9, 'So Moses made a serpent of bronze, and put it upon a pole; and whenever a serpent bit someone, that person would look at the serpent of bronze and live.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 10, 'The Israelites set out, and camped in Oboth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Journey to Moab'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 11, 'They set out from Oboth, and camped at Iye-abarim, in the wilderness bordering Moab toward the sunrise.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 12, 'From there they set out, and camped in the Wadi Zered.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 13, 'From there they set out, and camped on the other side of the Arnon, in the wilderness that extends from the boundary of the Amorites; for the Arnon is the boundary of Moab, between Moab and the Amorites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 14, 'Wherefore it is said in the Book of the Wars of the LORD,
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 1, 'The Israelites set out, and camped in the plains of Moab across the Jordan from Jericho.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Balak Summons Balaam to Curse Israel'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 2, 'Now Balak son of Zippor saw all that Israel had done to the Amorites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 3, 'Moab was in great dread of the people, because they were so numerous; Moab was overcome with fear of the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 4, 'And Moab said to the elders of Midian, "This horde will now lick up all that is around us, as an ox licks up the grass of the field." Now Balak son of Zippor was king of Moab at that time.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 5, 'He sent messengers to Balaam son of Beor at Pethor, which is on the Euphrates, in the land of Amaw, to summon him, saying, "A people has come out of Egypt; they have spread over the face of the earth, and they have settled next to me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 6, 'Come now, curse this people for me, since they are stronger than I; perhaps I shall be able to defeat them and drive them from the land; for I know that whomever you bless is blessed, and whomever you curse is cursed."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 7, 'So the elders of Moab and the elders of Midian departed with the fees for divination in their hand; and they came to Balaam, and gave him Balak"s message.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 8, 'He said to them, "Stay here tonight, and I will bring back word to you, just as the LORD speaks to me"; so the officials of Moab stayed with Balaam.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 9, 'God came to Balaam and said, "Who are these men with you?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 10, 'Balaam said to God, "King Balak son of Zippor of Moab, has sent me this message:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 11, '"A people has come out of Egypt and has spread over the face of the earth; now come, curse them for me; perhaps I shall be able to fight against them and drive them out.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 12, 'God said to Balaam, "You shall not go with them; you shall not curse the people, for they are blessed."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 13, 'So Balaam rose in the morning, and said to the officials of Balak, "Go to your own land, for the LORD has refused to let me go with you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 14, 'So the officials of Moab rose and went to Balak, and said, "Balaam refuses to come with us."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 15, 'Once again Balak sent officials, more numerous and more distinguished than these.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 16, 'They came to Balaam and said to him, "Thus says Balak son of Zippor: "Do not let anything hinder you from coming to me;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 17, 'for I will surely do you great honor, and whatever you say to me I will do; come, curse this people for me.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 18, 'But Balaam replied to the servants of Balak, "Although Balak were to give me his house full of silver and gold, I could not go beyond the command of the LORD my God, to do less or more.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 19, 'You remain here, as the others did, so that I may learn what more the LORD may say to me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 20, 'That night God came to Balaam and said to him, "If the men have come to summon you, get up and go with them; but do only what I tell you to do."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 21, 'So Balaam got up in the morning, saddled his donkey, and went with the officials of Moab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 22, 'God"s anger was kindled because he was going, and the angel of the LORD took his stand in the road as his adversary. Now he was riding on the donkey, and his two servants were with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Balaam, the Donkey, and the Angel'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 23, 'The donkey saw the angel of the LORD standing in the road, with a drawn sword in his hand; so the donkey turned off the road, and went into the field; and Balaam struck the donkey, to turn it back onto the road.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 24, 'Then the angel of the LORD stood in a narrow path between the vineyards, with a wall on either side.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 25, 'When the donkey saw the angel of the LORD, it scraped against the wall, and scraped Balaam"s foot against the wall; so he struck it again.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 26, 'Then the angel of the LORD went ahead, and stood in a narrow place, where there was no way to turn either to the right or to the left.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 27, 'When the donkey saw the angel of the LORD, it lay down under Balaam; and Balaam"s anger was kindled, and he struck the donkey with his staff.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 28, 'Then the LORD opened the mouth of the donkey, and it said to Balaam, "What have I done to you, that you have struck me these three times?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 29, 'Balaam said to the donkey, "Because you have made a fool of me! I wish I had a sword in my hand! I would kill you right now!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 30, 'But the donkey said to Balaam, "Am I not your donkey, which you have ridden all your life to this day? Have I been in the habit of treating you this way?" And he said, "No."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 31, 'Then the LORD opened the eyes of Balaam, and he saw the angel of the LORD standing in the road, with his drawn sword in his hand; and he bowed down, falling on his face.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 32, 'The angel of the LORD said to him, "Why have you struck your donkey these three times? I have come out as an adversary, because your way is perverse before me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 33, 'The donkey saw me, and turned away from me these three times. If it had not turned away from me, surely just now I would have killed you and let it live."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 34, 'Then Balaam said to the angel of the LORD, "I have sinned, for I did not know that you were standing in the road to oppose me. Now therefore, if it is displeasing to you, I will return home."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 35, 'The angel of the LORD said to Balaam, "Go with the men; but speak only what I tell you to speak." So Balaam went on with the officials of Balak.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 36, 'When Balak heard that Balaam had come, he went out to meet him at Ir-moab, on the boundary formed by the Arnon, at the farthest point of the boundary.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 37, 'Balak said to Balaam, "Did I not send to summon you? Why did you not come to me? Am I not able to honor you?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 38, 'Balaam said to Balak, "I have come to you now, but do I have power to say just anything? The word God puts in my mouth, that is what I must say."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 39, 'Then Balaam went with Balak, and they came to Kiriath-huzoth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 40, 'Balak sacrificed oxen and sheep, and sent them to Balaam and to the officials who were with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 22, 41, 'On the next day Balak took Balaam and brought him up to Bamoth-baal; and from there he could see part of the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Balaam"s First Oracle');
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 1, 'Then Balaam said to Balak, "Build me seven altars here, and prepare seven bulls and seven rams for me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 2, 'Balak did as Balaam had said; and Balak and Balaam offered a bull and a ram on each altar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 3, 'Then Balaam said to Balak, "Stay here beside your burnt offerings while I go aside. Perhaps the LORD will come to meet me. Whatever he shows me I will tell you." And he went to a bare height.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 4, 'Then God met Balaam; and Balaam said to him, "I have arranged the seven altars, and have offered a bull and a ram on each altar."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 5, 'The LORD put a word in Balaam"s mouth, and said, "Return to Balak, and this is what you must say."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 6, 'So he returned to Balak, who was standing beside his burnt offerings with all the officials of Moab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 7, 'Then Balaam uttered his oracle, saying:
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 1, 'Now Balaam saw that it pleased the LORD to bless Israel, so he did not go, as at other times, to look for omens, but set his face toward the wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Balaam"s Third Oracle'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 2, 'Balaam looked up and saw Israel camping tribe by tribe. Then the spirit of God came upon him,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 3, 'and he uttered his oracle, saying:
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 1, 'While Israel was staying at Shittim, the people began to have sexual relations with the women of Moab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Worship of Baal of Peor'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 2, 'These invited the people to the sacrifices of their gods, and the people ate and bowed down to their gods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 3, 'Thus Israel yoked itself to the Baal of Peor, and the LORD"s anger was kindled against Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 4, 'The LORD said to Moses, "Take all the chiefs of the people, and impale them in the sun before the LORD, in order that the fierce anger of the LORD may turn away from Israel."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 5, 'And Moses said to the judges of Israel, "Each of you shall kill any of your people who have yoked themselves to the Baal of Peor."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 6, 'Just then one of the Israelites came and brought a Midianite woman into his family, in the sight of Moses and in the sight of the whole congregation of the Israelites, while they were weeping at the entrance of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 7, 'When Phinehas son of Eleazar, son of Aaron the priest, saw it, he got up and left the congregation. Taking a spear in his hand,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 8, 'he went after the Israelite man into the tent, and pierced the two of them, the Israelite and the woman, through the belly. So the plague was stopped among the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 9, 'Nevertheless those that died by the plague were twenty-four thousand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 10, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 11, '"Phinehas son of Eleazar, son of Aaron the priest, has turned back my wrath from the Israelites by manifesting such zeal among them on my behalf that in my jealousy I did not consume the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 12, 'Therefore say, "I hereby grant him my covenant of peace.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 13, 'It shall be for him and for his descendants after him a covenant of perpetual priesthood, because he was zealous for his God, and made atonement for the Israelites.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 14, 'The name of the slain Israelite man, who was killed with the Midianite woman, was Zimri son of Salu, head of an ancestral house belonging to the Simeonites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 15, 'The name of the Midianite woman who was killed was Cozbi daughter of Zur, who was the head of a clan, an ancestral house in Midian.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 16, 'The LORD said to Moses,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 17, '"Harass the Midianites, and defeat them;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 25, 18, 'for they have harassed you by the trickery with which they deceived you in the affair of Peor, and in the affair of Cozbi, the daughter of a leader of Midian, their sister; she was killed on the day of the plague that resulted from Peor."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 1, 'After the plague the LORD said to Moses and to Eleazar son of Aaron the priest,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'A Census of the New Generation'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 2, '"Take a census of the whole congregation of the Israelites, from twenty years old and upward, by their ancestral houses, everyone in Israel able to go to war."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 3, 'Moses and Eleazar the priest spoke with them in the plains of Moab by the Jordan opposite Jericho, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 4, '"Take a census of the people, from twenty years old and upward," as the LORD commanded Moses.
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 1, 'Then the daughters of Zelophehad came forward. Zelophehad was son of Hepher son of Gilead son of Machir son of Manasseh son of Joseph, a member of the Manassite clans. The names of his daughters were: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Daughters of Zelophehad'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 2, 'They stood before Moses, Eleazar the priest, the leaders, and all the congregation, at the entrance of the tent of meeting, and they said,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 3, '"Our father died in the wilderness; he was not among the company of those who gathered themselves together against the LORD in the company of Korah, but died for his own sin; and he had no sons.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 4, 'Why should the name of our father be taken away from his clan because he had no son? Give to us a possession among our father"s brothers."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 5, 'Moses brought their case before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 6, 'And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 7, 'The daughters of Zelophehad are right in what they are saying; you shall indeed let them possess an inheritance among their father"s brothers and pass the inheritance of their father on to them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 8, 'You shall also say to the Israelites, "If a man dies, and has no son, then you shall pass his inheritance on to his daughter.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 9, 'If he has no daughter, then you shall give his inheritance to his brothers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 10, 'If he has no brothers, then you shall give his inheritance to his father"s brothers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 11, 'And if his father has no brothers, then you shall give his inheritance to the nearest kinsman of his clan, and he shall possess it. It shall be for the Israelites a statute and ordinance, as the LORD commanded Moses."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 12, 'The LORD said to Moses, "Go up this mountain of the Abarim range, and see the land that I have given to the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Joshua Appointed Moses" Successor'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 13, 'When you have seen it, you also shall be gathered to your people, as your brother Aaron was,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 14, 'because you rebelled against my word in the wilderness of Zin when the congregation quarreled with me. You did not show my holiness before their eyes at the waters." (These are the waters of Meribath-kadesh in the wilderness of Zin.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 15, 'Moses spoke to the LORD, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 16, '"Let the LORD, the God of the spirits of all flesh, appoint someone over the congregation', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 17, 'who shall go out before them and come in before them, who shall lead them out and bring them in, so that the congregation of the LORD may not be like sheep without a shepherd."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 18, 'So the LORD said to Moses, "Take Joshua son of Nun, a man in whom is the spirit, and lay your hand upon him;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 19, 'have him stand before Eleazar the priest and all the congregation, and commission him in their sight.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 20, 'You shall give him some of your authority, so that all the congregation of the Israelites may obey.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 21, 'But he shall stand before Eleazar the priest, who shall inquire for him by the decision of the Urim before the LORD; at his word they shall go out, and at his word they shall come in, both he and all the Israelites with him, the whole congregation."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 22, 'So Moses did as the LORD commanded him. He took Joshua and had him stand before Eleazar the priest and the whole congregation;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 27, 23, 'he laid his hands on him and commissioned him--as the LORD had directed through Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Daily Offerings'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 2, 'Command the Israelites, and say to them: My offering, the food for my offerings by fire, my pleasing odor, you shall take care to offer to me at its appointed time.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 3, 'And you shall say to them, This is the offering by fire that you shall offer to the LORD: two male lambs a year old without blemish, daily, as a regular offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 4, 'One lamb you shall offer in the morning, and the other lamb you shall offer at twilight;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 5, 'also one-tenth of an ephah of choice flour for a grain offering, mixed with one-fourth of a hin of beaten oil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 6, 'It is a regular burnt offering, ordained at Mount Sinai for a pleasing odor, an offering by fire to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 7, 'Its drink offering shall be one-fourth of a hin for each lamb; in the sanctuary you shall pour out a drink offering of strong drink to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 8, 'The other lamb you shall offer at twilight with a grain offering and a drink offering like the one in the morning; you shall offer it as an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 9, 'On the sabbath day: two male lambs a year old without blemish, and two-tenths of an ephah of choice flour for a grain offering, mixed with oil, and its drink offering--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Sabbath Offerings'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 10, 'this is the burnt offering for every sabbath, in addition to the regular burnt offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 11, 'At the beginnings of your months you shall offer a burnt offering to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without blemish;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Monthly Offerings'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 12, 'also three-tenths of an ephah of choice flour for a grain offering, mixed with oil, for each bull; and two-tenths of choice flour for a grain offering, mixed with oil, for the one ram;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 13, 'and one-tenth of choice flour mixed with oil as a grain offering for every lamb--a burnt offering of pleasing odor, an offering by fire to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 14, 'Their drink offerings shall be half a hin of wine for a bull, one-third of a hin for a ram, and one-fourth of a hin for a lamb. This is the burnt offering of every month throughout the months of the year.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 15, 'And there shall be one male goat for a sin offering to the LORD; it shall be offered in addition to the regular burnt offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 16, 'On the fourteenth day of the first month there shall be a passover offering to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Offerings at Passover'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 17, 'And on the fifteenth day of this month is a festival; seven days shall unleavened bread be eaten.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 18, 'On the first day there shall be a holy convocation. You shall not work at your occupations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 19, 'You shall offer an offering by fire, a burnt offering to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old; see that they are without blemish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 20, 'Their grain offering shall be of choice flour mixed with oil: three-tenths of an ephah shall you offer for a bull, and two-tenths for a ram;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 21, 'one-tenth shall you offer for each of the seven lambs;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 22, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, to make atonement for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 23, 'You shall offer these in addition to the burnt offering of the morning, which belongs to the regular burnt offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 24, 'In the same way you shall offer daily, for seven days, the food of an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD; it shall be offered in addition to the regular burnt offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 25, 'And on the seventh day you shall have a holy convocation; you shall not work at your occupations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 26, 'On the day of the first fruits, when you offer a grain offering of new grain to the LORD at your festival of weeks, you shall have a holy convocation; you shall not work at your occupations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Offerings at the Festival of Weeks'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 27, 'You shall offer a burnt offering, a pleasing odor to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, seven male lambs a year old.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 28, 'Their grain offering shall be of choice flour mixed with oil, three-tenths of an ephah for each bull, two-tenths for one ram,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 29, 'one-tenth for each of the seven lambs;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 30, 'with one male goat, to make atonement for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 28, 31, 'In addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering, you shall offer them and their drink offering. They shall be without blemish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 1, 'On the first day of the seventh month you shall have a holy convocation; you shall not work at your occupations. It is a day for you to blow the trumpets,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Offerings at the Festival of Trumpets'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 2, 'and you shall offer a burnt offering, a pleasing odor to the LORD: one young bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without blemish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 3, 'Their grain offering shall be of choice flour mixed with oil, three-tenths of one ephah for the bull, two-tenths for the ram,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 4, 'and one-tenth for each of the seven lambs;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 5, 'with one male goat for a sin offering, to make atonement for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 6, 'These are in addition to the burnt offering of the new moon and its grain offering, and the regular burnt offering and its grain offering, and their drink offerings, according to the ordinance for them, a pleasing odor, an offering by fire to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 7, 'On the tenth day of this seventh month you shall have a holy convocation, and deny yourselves; you shall do no work.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Offerings on the Day of Atonement'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 8, 'You shall offer a burnt offering to the LORD, a pleasing odor: one young bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old. They shall be without blemish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 9, 'Their grain offering shall be of choice flour mixed with oil, three-tenths of an ephah for the bull, two-tenths for the one ram,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 10, 'one-tenth for each of the seven lambs;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 11, 'with one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the sin offering of atonement, and the regular burnt offering and its grain offering, and their drink offerings.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 12, 'On the fifteenth day of the seventh month you shall have a holy convocation; you shall not work at your occupations. You shall celebrate a festival to the LORD seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Offerings at the Festival of Booths'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 13, 'You shall offer a burnt offering, an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD: thirteen young bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old. They shall be without blemish.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 14, 'Their grain offering shall be of choice flour mixed with oil, three-tenths of an ephah for each of the thirteen bulls, two-tenths for each of the two rams,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 15, 'and one-tenth for each of the fourteen lambs;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 16, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering, its grain offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 17, 'On the second day: twelve young bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 18, 'with the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 19, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering and its grain offering, and their drink offerings.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 20, 'On the third day: eleven bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 21, 'with the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 22, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering and its grain offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 23, 'On the fourth day: ten bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 24, 'with the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 25, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering, its grain offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 26, 'On the fifth day: nine bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 27, 'with the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 28, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering and its grain offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 29, 'On the sixth day: eight bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 30, 'with the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 31, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering, its grain offering, and its drink offerings.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 32, 'On the seventh day: seven bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 33, 'with the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 34, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, besides the regular burnt offering, its grain offering, and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 35, 'On the eighth day you shall have a solemn assembly; you shall not work at your occupations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 36, 'You shall offer a burnt offering, an offering by fire, a pleasing odor to the LORD: one bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without blemish,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 37, 'and the grain offering and the drink offerings for the bull, for the ram, and for the lambs, as prescribed in accordance with their number;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 38, 'also one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering and its grain offering and its drink offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 39, 'These you shall offer to the LORD at your appointed festivals, in addition to your votive offerings and your freewill offerings, as your burnt offerings, your grain offerings, your drink offerings, and your offerings of well-being.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 29, 40, 'So Moses told the Israelites everything just as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 1, 'Then Moses said to the heads of the tribes of the Israelites: This is what the LORD has commanded.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Vows Made by Women'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 2, 'When a man makes a vow to the LORD, or swears an oath to bind himself by a pledge, he shall not break his word; he shall do according to all that proceeds out of his mouth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 3, 'When a woman makes a vow to the LORD, or binds herself by a pledge, while within her father"s house, in her youth,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 4, 'and her father hears of her vow or her pledge by which she has bound herself, and says nothing to her; then all her vows shall stand, and any pledge by which she has bound herself shall stand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 5, 'But if her father expresses disapproval to her at the time that he hears of it, no vow of hers, and no pledge by which she has bound herself, shall stand; and the LORD will forgive her, because her father had expressed to her his disapproval.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 6, 'If she marries, while obligated by her vows or any thoughtless utterance of her lips by which she has bound herself,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 7, 'and her husband hears of it and says nothing to her at the time that he hears, then her vows shall stand, and her pledges by which she has bound herself shall stand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 8, 'But if, at the time that her husband hears of it, he expresses disapproval to her, then he shall nullify the vow by which she was obligated, or the thoughtless utterance of her lips, by which she bound herself; and the LORD will forgive her.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 9, '(But every vow of a widow or of a divorced woman, by which she has bound herself, shall be binding upon her.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 10, 'And if she made a vow in her husband"s house, or bound herself by a pledge with an oath,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 11, 'and her husband heard it and said nothing to her, and did not express disapproval to her, then all her vows shall stand, and any pledge by which she bound herself shall stand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 12, 'But if her husband nullifies them at the time that he hears them, then whatever proceeds out of her lips concerning her vows, or concerning her pledge of herself, shall not stand. Her husband has nullified them, and the LORD will forgive her.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 13, 'Any vow or any binding oath to deny herself, her husband may allow to stand, or her husband may nullify.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 14, 'But if her husband says nothing to her from day to day, then he validates all her vows, or all her pledges, by which she is obligated; he has validated them, because he said nothing to her at the time that he heard of them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 15, 'But if he nullifies them some time after he has heard of them, then he shall bear her guilt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 30, 16, 'These are the statutes that the LORD commanded Moses concerning a husband and his wife, and a father and his daughter while she is still young and in her father"s house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'War against Midian'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 2, '"Avenge the Israelites on the Midianites; afterward you shall be gathered to your people."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 3, 'So Moses said to the people, "Arm some of your number for the war, so that they may go against Midian, to execute the LORD"s vengeance on Midian.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 4, 'You shall send a thousand from each of the tribes of Israel to the war."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 5, 'So out of the thousands of Israel, a thousand from each tribe were conscripted, twelve thousand armed for battle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 6, 'Moses sent them to the war, a thousand from each tribe, along with Phinehas son of Eleazar the priest, with the vessels of the sanctuary and the trumpets for sounding the alarm in his hand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 7, 'They did battle against Midian, as the LORD had commanded Moses, and killed every male.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 8, 'They killed the kings of Midian: Evi, Rekem, Zur, Hur, and Reba, the five kings of Midian, in addition to others who were slain by them; and they also killed Balaam son of Beor with the sword.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 9, 'The Israelites took the women of Midian and their little ones captive; and they took all their cattle, their flocks, and all their goods as booty.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 10, 'All their towns where they had settled, and all their encampments, they burned,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 11, 'but they took all the spoil and all the booty, both people and animals.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 12, 'Then they brought the captives and the booty and the spoil to Moses, to Eleazar the priest, and to the congregation of the Israelites, at the camp on the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 13, 'Moses, Eleazar the priest, and all the leaders of the congregation went to meet them outside the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Return from the War'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 14, 'Moses became angry with the officers of the army, the commanders of thousands and the commanders of hundreds, who had come from service in the war.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 15, 'Moses said to them, "Have you allowed all the women to live?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 16, 'These women here, on Balaam"s advice, made the Israelites act treacherously against the LORD in the affair of Peor, so that the plague came among the congregation of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 17, 'Now therefore, kill every male among the little ones, and kill every woman who has known a man by sleeping with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 18, 'But all the young girls who have not known a man by sleeping with him, keep alive for yourselves.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 19, 'Camp outside the camp seven days; whoever of you has killed any person or touched a corpse, purify yourselves and your captives on the third and on the seventh day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 20, 'You shall purify every garment, every article of skin, everything made of goats" hair, and every article of wood."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 21, 'Eleazar the priest said to the troops who had gone to battle: "This is the statute of the law that the LORD has commanded Moses:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 22, 'gold, silver, bronze, iron, tin, and lead--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 23, 'everything that can withstand fire, shall be passed through fire, and it shall be clean. Nevertheless it shall also be purified with the water for purification; and whatever cannot withstand fire, shall be passed through the water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 24, 'You must wash your clothes on the seventh day, and you shall be clean; afterward you may come into the camp."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 25, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Disposition of Captives and Booty'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 26, '"You and Eleazar the priest and the heads of the ancestral houses of the congregation make an inventory of the booty captured, both human and animal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 27, 'Divide the booty into two parts, between the warriors who went out to battle and all the congregation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 28, 'From the share of the warriors who went out to battle, set aside as tribute for the LORD, one item out of every five hundred, whether persons, oxen, donkeys, sheep, or goats.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 29, 'Take it from their half and give it to Eleazar the priest as an offering to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 30, 'But from the Israelites" half you shall take one out of every fifty, whether persons, oxen, donkeys, sheep, or goats--all the animals--and give them to the Levites who have charge of the tabernacle of the LORD."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 31, 'Then Moses and Eleazar the priest did as the LORD had commanded Moses:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 32, 'The booty remaining from the spoil that the troops had taken totaled six hundred seventy-five thousand sheep,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 33, 'seventy-two thousand oxen,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 34, 'sixty-one thousand donkeys,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 35, 'and thirty-two thousand persons in all, women who had not known a man by sleeping with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 36, 'The half-share, the portion of those who had gone out to war, was in number three hundred thirty-seven thousand five hundred sheep and goats,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 37, 'and the LORD"s tribute of sheep and goats was six hundred seventy-five.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 38, 'The oxen were thirty-six thousand, of which the LORD"s tribute was seventy-two.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 39, 'The donkeys were thirty thousand five hundred, of which the LORD"s tribute was sixty-one.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 40, 'The persons were sixteen thousand, of which the LORD"s tribute was thirty-two persons.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 41, 'Moses gave the tribute, the offering for the LORD, to Eleazar the priest, as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 42, 'As for the Israelites" half, which Moses separated from that of the troops,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 43, 'the congregation"s half was three hundred thirty-seven thousand five hundred sheep and goats,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 44, 'thirty-six thousand oxen,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 45, 'thirty thousand five hundred donkeys,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 46, 'and sixteen thousand persons.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 47, 'From the Israelites" half Moses took one of every fifty, both of persons and of animals, and gave them to the Levites who had charge of the tabernacle of the LORD; as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 48, 'Then the officers who were over the thousands of the army, the commanders of thousands and the commanders of hundreds, approached Moses,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 49, 'and said to Moses, "Your servants have counted the warriors who are under our command, and not one of us is missing.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 50, 'And we have brought the LORD"s offering, what each of us found, articles of gold, armlets and bracelets, signet rings, earrings, and pendants, to make atonement for ourselves before the LORD."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 51, 'Moses and Eleazar the priest received the gold from them, all in the form of crafted articles.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 52, 'And all the gold of the offering that they offered to the LORD, from the commanders of thousands and the commanders of hundreds, was sixteen thousand seven hundred fifty shekels.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 53, '(The troops had all taken plunder for themselves.)', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 31, 54, 'So Moses and Eleazar the priest received the gold from the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and brought it into the tent of meeting as a memorial for the Israelites before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 1, 'Now the Reubenites and the Gadites owned a very great number of cattle. When they saw that the land of Jazer and the land of Gilead was a good place for cattle,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Conquest and Division of Transjordan'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 2, 'the Gadites and the Reubenites came and spoke to Moses, to Eleazar the priest, and to the leaders of the congregation, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 3, '"Ataroth, Dibon, Jazer, Nimrah, Heshbon, Elealeh, Sebam, Nebo, and Beon--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 4, 'the land that the LORD subdued before the congregation of Israel--is a land for cattle; and your servants have cattle."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 5, 'They continued, "If we have found favor in your sight, let this land be given to your servants for a possession; do not make us cross the Jordan."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 6, 'But Moses said to the Gadites and to the Reubenites, "Shall your brothers go to war while you sit here?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 7, 'Why will you discourage the hearts of the Israelites from going over into the land that the LORD has given them?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 8, 'Your fathers did this, when I sent them from Kadesh-barnea to see the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 9, 'When they went up to the Wadi Eshcol and saw the land, they discouraged the hearts of the Israelites from going into the land that the LORD had given them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 10, 'The LORD"s anger was kindled on that day and he swore, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 11, '"Surely none of the people who came up out of Egypt, from twenty years old and upward, shall see the land that I swore to give to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, because they have not unreservedly followed me--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 12, 'none except Caleb son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite and Joshua son of Nun, for they have unreservedly followed the LORD."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 13, 'And the LORD"s anger was kindled against Israel, and he made them wander in the wilderness for forty years, until all the generation that had done evil in the sight of the LORD had disappeared.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 14, 'And now you, a brood of sinners, have risen in place of your fathers, to increase the LORD"s fierce anger against Israel!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 15, 'If you turn away from following him, he will again abandon them in the wilderness; and you will destroy all this people."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 16, 'Then they came up to him and said, "We will build sheepfolds here for our flocks, and towns for our little ones,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 17, 'but we will take up arms as a vanguard before the Israelites, until we have brought them to their place. Meanwhile our little ones will stay in the fortified towns because of the inhabitants of the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 18, 'We will not return to our homes until all the Israelites have obtained their inheritance.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 19, 'We will not inherit with them on the other side of the Jordan and beyond, because our inheritance has come to us on this side of the Jordan to the east."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 20, 'So Moses said to them, "If you do this--if you take up arms to go before the LORD for the war,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 21, 'and all those of you who bear arms cross the Jordan before the LORD, until he has driven out his enemies from before him', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 22, 'and the land is subdued before the LORD--then after that you may return and be free of obligation to the LORD and to Israel, and this land shall be your possession before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 23, 'But if you do not do this, you have sinned against the LORD; and be sure your sin will find you out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 24, 'Build towns for your little ones, and folds for your flocks; but do what you have promised."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 25, 'Then the Gadites and the Reubenites said to Moses, "Your servants will do as my lord commands.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 26, 'Our little ones, our wives, our flocks, and all our livestock shall remain there in the towns of Gilead;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 27, 'but your servants will cross over, everyone armed for war, to do battle for the LORD, just as my lord orders."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 28, 'So Moses gave command concerning them to Eleazar the priest, to Joshua son of Nun, and to the heads of the ancestral houses of the Israelite tribes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 29, 'And Moses said to them, "If the Gadites and the Reubenites, everyone armed for battle before the LORD, will cross over the Jordan with you and the land shall be subdued before you, then you shall give them the land of Gilead for a possession;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 30, 'but if they will not cross over with you armed, they shall have possessions among you in the land of Canaan."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 31, 'The Gadites and the Reubenites answered, "As the LORD has spoken to your servants, so we will do.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 32, 'We will cross over armed before the LORD into the land of Canaan, but the possession of our inheritance shall remain with us on this side of the Jordan."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 33, 'Moses gave to them--to the Gadites and to the Reubenites and to the half-tribe of Manasseh son of Joseph--the kingdom of King Sihon of the Amorites and the kingdom of King Og of Bashan, the land and its towns, with the territories of the surrounding towns.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 34, 'And the Gadites rebuilt Dibon, Ataroth, Aroer,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 35, 'Atroth-shophan, Jazer, Jogbehah,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 36, 'Beth-nimrah, and Beth-haran, fortified cities, and folds for sheep.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 37, 'And the Reubenites rebuilt Heshbon, Elealeh, Kiriathaim,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 38, 'Nebo, and Baal-meon (some names being changed), and Sibmah; and they gave names to the towns that they rebuilt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 39, 'The descendants of Machir son of Manasseh went to Gilead, captured it, and dispossessed the Amorites who were there;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 40, 'so Moses gave Gilead to Machir son of Manasseh, and he settled there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 41, 'Jair son of Manasseh went and captured their villages, and renamed them Havvoth-jair.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 32, 42, 'And Nobah went and captured Kenath and its villages, and renamed it Nobah after himself.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 1, 'These are the stages by which the Israelites went out of the land of Egypt in military formation under the leadership of Moses and Aaron.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Stages of Israel"s Journey from Egypt'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 2, 'Moses wrote down their starting points, stage by stage, by command of the LORD; and these are their stages according to their starting places.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 3, 'They set out from Rameses in the first month, on the fifteenth day of the first month; on the day after the passover the Israelites went out boldly in the sight of all the Egyptians,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 4, 'while the Egyptians were burying all their firstborn, whom the LORD had struck down among them. The LORD executed judgments even against their gods.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 5, 'So the Israelites set out from Rameses, and camped at Succoth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 6, 'They set out from Succoth, and camped at Etham, which is on the edge of the wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 7, 'They set out from Etham, and turned back to Pi-hahiroth, which faces Baal-zephon; and they camped before Migdol.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 8, 'They set out from Pi-hahiroth, passed through the sea into the wilderness, went a three days" journey in the wilderness of Etham, and camped at Marah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 9, 'They set out from Marah and came to Elim; at Elim there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees, and they camped there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 10, 'They set out from Elim and camped by the Red Sea.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 11, 'They set out from the Red Sea and camped in the wilderness of Sin.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 12, 'They set out from the wilderness of Sin and camped at Dophkah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 13, 'They set out from Dophkah and camped at Alush.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 14, 'They set out from Alush and camped at Rephidim, where there was no water for the people to drink.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 15, 'They set out from Rephidim and camped in the wilderness of Sinai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 16, 'They set out from the wilderness of Sinai and camped at Kibroth-hattaavah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 17, 'They set out from Kibroth-hattaavah and camped at Hazeroth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 18, 'They set out from Hazeroth and camped at Rithmah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 19, 'They set out from Rithmah and camped at Rimmon-perez.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 20, 'They set out from Rimmon-perez and camped at Libnah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 21, 'They set out from Libnah and camped at Rissah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 22, 'They set out from Rissah and camped at Kehelathah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 23, 'They set out from Kehelathah and camped at Mount Shepher.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 24, 'They set out from Mount Shepher and camped at Haradah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 25, 'They set out from Haradah and camped at Makheloth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 26, 'They set out from Makheloth and camped at Tahath.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 27, 'They set out from Tahath and camped at Terah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 28, 'They set out from Terah and camped at Mithkah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 29, 'They set out from Mithkah and camped at Hashmonah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 30, 'They set out from Hashmonah and camped at Moseroth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 31, 'They set out from Moseroth and camped at Bene-jaakan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 32, 'They set out from Bene-jaakan and camped at Hor-haggidgad.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 33, 'They set out from Hor-haggidgad and camped at Jotbathah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 34, 'They set out from Jotbathah and camped at Abronah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 35, 'They set out from Abronah and camped at Ezion-geber.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 36, 'They set out from Ezion-geber and camped in the wilderness of Zin (that is, Kadesh).', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 37, 'They set out from Kadesh and camped at Mount Hor, on the edge of the land of Edom.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 38, 'Aaron the priest went up Mount Hor at the command of the LORD and died there in the fortieth year after the Israelites had come out of the land of Egypt, on the first day of the fifth month.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 39, 'Aaron was one hundred twenty-three years old when he died on Mount Hor.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 40, 'The Canaanite, the king of Arad, who lived in the Negeb in the land of Canaan, heard of the coming of the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 41, 'They set out from Mount Hor and camped at Zalmonah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 42, 'They set out from Zalmonah and camped at Punon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 43, 'They set out from Punon and camped at Oboth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 44, 'They set out from Oboth and camped at Iye-abarim, in the territory of Moab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 45, 'They set out from Iyim and camped at Dibon-gad.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 46, 'They set out from Dibon-gad and camped at Almon-diblathaim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 47, 'They set out from Almon-diblathaim and camped in the mountains of Abarim, before Nebo.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 48, 'They set out from the mountains of Abarim and camped in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 49, 'they camped by the Jordan from Beth-jeshimoth as far as Abel-shittim in the plains of Moab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 50, 'In the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho, the LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Directions for the Conquest of Canaan'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 51, 'Speak to the Israelites, and say to them: When you cross over the Jordan into the land of Canaan,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 52, 'you shall drive out all the inhabitants of the land from before you, destroy all their figured stones, destroy all their cast images, and demolish all their high places.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 53, 'You shall take possession of the land and settle in it, for I have given you the land to possess.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 54, 'You shall apportion the land by lot according to your clans; to a large one you shall give a large inheritance, and to a small one you shall give a small inheritance; the inheritance shall belong to the person on whom the lot falls; according to your ancestral tribes you shall inherit.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 55, 'But if you do not drive out the inhabitants of the land from before you, then those whom you let remain shall be as barbs in your eyes and thorns in your sides; they shall trouble you in the land where you are settling.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 33, 56, 'And I will do to you as I thought to do to them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 1, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Boundaries of the Land'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 2, 'Command the Israelites, and say to them: When you enter the land of Canaan (this is the land that shall fall to you for an inheritance, the land of Canaan, defined by its boundaries),', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 3, 'your south sector shall extend from the wilderness of Zin along the side of Edom. Your southern boundary shall begin from the end of the Dead Sea on the east;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 4, 'your boundary shall turn south of the ascent of Akrabbim, and cross to Zin, and its outer limit shall be south of Kadesh-barnea; then it shall go on to Hazar-addar, and cross to Azmon;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 5, 'the boundary shall turn from Azmon to the Wadi of Egypt, and its termination shall be at the Sea.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 6, 'For the western boundary, you shall have the Great Sea and its coast; this shall be your western boundary.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 7, 'This shall be your northern boundary: from the Great Sea you shall mark out your line to Mount Hor;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 8, 'from Mount Hor you shall mark it out to Lebo-hamath, and the outer limit of the boundary shall be at Zedad;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 9, 'then the boundary shall extend to Ziphron, and its end shall be at Hazar-enan; this shall be your northern boundary.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 10, 'You shall mark out your eastern boundary from Hazar-enan to Shepham;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 11, 'and the boundary shall continue down from Shepham to Riblah on the east side of Ain; and the boundary shall go down, and reach the eastern slope of the sea of Chinnereth;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 12, 'and the boundary shall go down to the Jordan, and its end shall be at the Dead Sea. This shall be your land with its boundaries all around.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 13, 'Moses commanded the Israelites, saying: This is the land that you shall inherit by lot, which the LORD has commanded to give to the nine tribes and to the half-tribe;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 14, 'for the tribe of the Reubenites by their ancestral houses and the tribe of the Gadites by their ancestral houses have taken their inheritance, and also the half-tribe of Manasseh;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 15, 'the two tribes and the half-tribe have taken their inheritance beyond the Jordan at Jericho eastward, toward the sunrise.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 16, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Tribal Leaders'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 17, 'These are the names of the men who shall apportion the land to you for inheritance: the priest Eleazar and Joshua son of Nun.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 18, 'You shall take one leader of every tribe to apportion the land for inheritance.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 19, 'These are the names of the men: Of the tribe of Judah, Caleb son of Jephunneh.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 20, 'Of the tribe of the Simeonites, Shemuel son of Ammihud.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 21, 'Of the tribe of Benjamin, Elidad son of Chislon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 22, 'Of the tribe of the Danites a leader, Bukki son of Jogli.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 23, 'Of the Josephites: of the tribe of the Manassites a leader, Hanniel son of Ephod,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 24, 'and of the tribe of the Ephraimites a leader, Kemuel son of Shiphtan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 25, 'Of the tribe of the Zebulunites a leader, Eli-zaphan son of Parnach.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 26, 'Of the tribe of the Issacharites a leader, Paltiel son of Azzan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 27, 'And of the tribe of the Asherites a leader, Ahihud son of Shelomi.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 28, 'Of the tribe of the Naphtalites a leader, Pedahel son of Ammihud.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 34, 29, 'These were the ones whom the LORD commanded to apportion the inheritance for the Israelites in the land of Canaan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 1, 'In the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho, the LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Cities for the Levites'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 2, 'Command the Israelites to give, from the inheritance that they possess, towns for the Levites to live in; you shall also give to the Levites pasture lands surrounding the towns.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 3, 'The towns shall be theirs to live in, and their pasture lands shall be for their cattle, for their livestock, and for all their animals.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 4, 'The pasture lands of the towns, which you shall give to the Levites, shall reach from the wall of the town outward a thousand cubits all around.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 5, 'You shall measure, outside the town, for the east side two thousand cubits, for the south side two thousand cubits, for the west side two thousand cubits, and for the north side two thousand cubits, with the town in the middle; this shall belong to them as pasture land for their towns.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 6, 'The towns that you give to the Levites shall include the six cities of refuge, where you shall permit a slayer to flee, and in addition to them you shall give forty-two towns.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 7, 'The towns that you give to the Levites shall total forty-eight, with their pasture lands.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 8, 'And as for the towns that you shall give from the possession of the Israelites, from the larger tribes you shall take many, and from the smaller tribes you shall take few; each, in proportion to the inheritance that it obtains, shall give of its towns to the Levites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 9, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Cities of Refuge'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 10, 'Speak to the Israelites, and say to them: When you cross the Jordan into the land of Canaan,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 11, 'then you shall select cities to be cities of refuge for you, so that a slayer who kills a person without intent may flee there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 12, 'The cities shall be for you a refuge from the avenger, so that the slayer may not die until there is a trial before the congregation.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 13, 'The cities that you designate shall be six cities of refuge for you:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 14, 'you shall designate three cities beyond the Jordan, and three cities in the land of Canaan, to be cities of refuge.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 15, 'These six cities shall serve as refuge for the Israelites, for the resident or transient alien among them, so that anyone who kills a person without intent may flee there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 16, 'But anyone who strikes another with an iron object, and death ensues, is a murderer; the murderer shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Concerning Murder and Blood Revenge'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 17, 'Or anyone who strikes another with a stone in hand that could cause death, and death ensues, is a murderer; the murderer shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 18, 'Or anyone who strikes another with a weapon of wood in hand that could cause death, and death ensues, is a murderer; the murderer shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 19, 'The avenger of blood is the one who shall put the murderer to death; when they meet, the avenger of blood shall execute the sentence.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 20, 'Likewise, if someone pushes another from hatred, or hurls something at another, lying in wait, and death ensues,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 21, 'or in enmity strikes another with the hand, and death ensues, then the one who struck the blow shall be put to death; that person is a murderer; the avenger of blood shall put the murderer to death, when they meet.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 22, 'But if someone pushes another suddenly without enmity, or hurls any object without lying in wait,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 23, 'or, while handling any stone that could cause death, unintentionally drops it on another and death ensues, though they were not enemies, and no harm was intended,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 24, 'then the congregation shall judge between the slayer and the avenger of blood, in accordance with these ordinances;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 25, 'and the congregation shall rescue the slayer from the avenger of blood. Then the congregation shall send the slayer back to the original city of refuge. The slayer shall live in it until the death of the high priest who was anointed with the holy oil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 26, 'But if the slayer shall at any time go outside the bounds of the original city of refuge,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 27, 'and is found by the avenger of blood outside the bounds of the city of refuge, and is killed by the avenger, no bloodguilt shall be incurred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 28, 'For the slayer must remain in the city of refuge until the death of the high priest; but after the death of the high priest the slayer may return home.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 29, 'These things shall be a statute and ordinance for you throughout your generations wherever you live.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 30, 'If anyone kills another, the murderer shall be put to death on the evidence of witnesses; but no one shall be put to death on the testimony of a single witness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 31, 'Moreover you shall accept no ransom for the life of a murderer who is subject to the death penalty; a murderer must be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 32, 'Nor shall you accept ransom for one who has fled to a city of refuge, enabling the fugitive to return to live in the land before the death of the high priest.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 33, 'You shall not pollute the land in which you live; for blood pollutes the land, and no expiation can be made for the land, for the blood that is shed in it, except by the blood of the one who shed it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 35, 34, 'You shall not defile the land in which you live, in which I also dwell; for I the LORD dwell among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.bible_verses (book_no, book_abbr, book_name, chapter, verse, content, language, translation, title) VALUES
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 1, 'The heads of the ancestral houses of the clans of the descendants of Gilead son of Machir son of Manasseh, of the Josephite clans, came forward and spoke in the presence of Moses and the leaders, the heads of the ancestral houses of the Israelites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Marriage of Female Heirs'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 2, 'they said, "The LORD commanded my lord to give the land for inheritance by lot to the Israelites; and my lord was commanded by the LORD to give the inheritance of our brother Zelophehad to his daughters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 3, 'But if they are married into another Israelite tribe, then their inheritance will be taken from the inheritance of our ancestors and added to the inheritance of the tribe into which they marry; so it will be taken away from the allotted portion of our inheritance.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 4, 'And when the jubilee of the Israelites comes, then their inheritance will be added to the inheritance of the tribe into which they have married; and their inheritance will be taken from the inheritance of our ancestral tribe."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 5, 'Then Moses commanded the Israelites according to the word of the LORD, saying, "The descendants of the tribe of Joseph are right in what they are saying.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 6, 'This is what the LORD commands concerning the daughters of Zelophehad, "Let them marry whom they think best; only it must be into a clan of their father"s tribe that they are married,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 7, 'so that no inheritance of the Israelites shall be transferred from one tribe to another; for all Israelites shall retain the inheritance of their ancestral tribes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 8, 'Every daughter who possesses an inheritance in any tribe of the Israelites shall marry one from the clan of her father"s tribe, so that all Israelites may continue to possess their ancestral inheritance.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 9, 'No inheritance shall be transferred from one tribe to another; for each of the tribes of the Israelites shall retain its own inheritance.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 10, 'The daughters of Zelophehad did as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 11, 'Mahlah, Tirzah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Noah, the daughters of Zelophehad, married sons of their father"s brothers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 12, 'They were married into the clans of the descendants of Manasseh son of Joseph, and their inheritance remained in the tribe of their father"s clan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 36, 13, 'These are the commandments and the ordinances that the LORD commanded through Moses to the Israelites in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);
