-- NRSV-CE OLD TESTAMENT BIBLE VERSES (PART 2)



All fat is the LORD"s.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 3, 17, 'It shall be a perpetual statute throughout your generations, in all your settlements: you must not eat any fat or any blood.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);







"Through those who are near me  
    I will show myself holy,  
and before all the people  
    I will be glorified.""
And Aaron was silent.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 4, 'Moses summoned Mishael and Elzaphan, sons of Uzziel the uncle of Aaron, and said to them, "Come forward, and carry your kinsmen away from the front of the sanctuary to a place outside the camp."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 5, 'They came forward and carried them by their tunics out of the camp, as Moses had ordered.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 6, 'And Moses said to Aaron and to his sons Eleazar and Ithamar, "Do not dishevel your hair, and do not tear your vestments, or you will die and wrath will strike all the congregation; but your kindred, the whole house of Israel, may mourn the burning that the LORD has sent.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 7, 'You shall not go outside the entrance of the tent of meeting, or you will die; for the anointing oil of the LORD is on you." And they did as Moses had ordered.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 8, 'And the LORD spoke to Aaron:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 9, 'Drink no wine or strong drink, neither you nor your sons, when you enter the tent of meeting, that you may not die; it is a statute forever throughout your generations.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 10, 'You are to distinguish between the holy and the common, and between the unclean and the clean;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 11, 'and you are to teach the people of Israel all the statutes that the LORD has spoken to them through Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 12, 'Moses spoke to Aaron and to his remaining sons, Eleazar and Ithamar: Take the grain offering that is left from the LORD"s offerings by fire, and eat it unleavened beside the altar, for it is most holy;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 13, 'you shall eat it in a holy place, because it is your due and your sons" due, from the offerings by fire to the LORD; for so I am commanded.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 14, 'But the breast that is elevated and the thigh that is raised, you and your sons and daughters as well may eat in any clean place; for they have been assigned to you and your children from the sacrifices of the offerings of well-being of the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 15, 'The thigh that is raised and the breast that is elevated they shall bring, together with the offerings by fire of the fat, to raise for an elevation offering before the LORD; they are to be your due and that of your children forever, as the LORD has commanded.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 16, 'Then Moses made inquiry about the goat of the sin offering, and--it had already been burned! He was angry with Eleazar and Ithamar, Aaron"s remaining sons, and said,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 17, '"Why did you not eat the sin offering in the sacred area? For it is most holy, and God has given it to you that you may remove the guilt of the congregation, to make atonement on their behalf before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 18, 'Its blood was not brought into the inner part of the sanctuary. You should certainly have eaten it in the sanctuary, as I commanded."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 19, 'And Aaron spoke to Moses, "See, today they offered their sin offering and their burnt offering before the LORD; and yet such things as these have befallen me! If I had eaten the sin offering today, would it have been agreeable to the LORD?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 10, 20, 'And when Moses heard that, he agreed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

From among all the land animals, these are the creatures that you may eat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 3, 'Any animal that has divided hoofs and is cleft-footed and chews the cud--such you may eat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 4, 'But among those that chew the cud or have divided hoofs, you shall not eat the following: the camel, for even though it chews the cud, it does not have divided hoofs; it is unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 5, 'The rock badger, for even though it chews the cud, it does not have divided hoofs; it is unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 6, 'The hare, for even though it chews the cud, it does not have divided hoofs; it is unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 7, 'The pig, for even though it has divided hoofs and is cleft-footed, it does not chew the cud; it is unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 8, 'Of their flesh you shall not eat, and their carcasses you shall not touch; they are unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 9, 'These you may eat, of all that are in the waters. Everything in the waters that has fins and scales, whether in the seas or in the streams--such you may eat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 10, 'But anything in the seas or the streams that does not have fins and scales, of the swarming creatures in the waters and among all the other living creatures that are in the waters--they are detestable to you', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 11, 'and detestable they shall remain. Of their flesh you shall not eat, and their carcasses you shall regard as detestable.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 12, 'Everything in the waters that does not have fins and scales is detestable to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 13, 'These you shall regard as detestable among the birds. They shall not be eaten; they are an abomination: the eagle, the vulture, the osprey,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 14, 'the buzzard, the kite of any kind;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 15, 'every raven of any kind;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 16, 'the ostrich, the nighthawk, the sea gull, the hawk of any kind;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 17, 'the little owl, the cormorant, the great owl,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 18, 'the water hen, the desert owl, the carrion vulture,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 19, 'the stork, the heron of any kind, the hoopoe, and the bat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 20, 'All winged insects that walk upon all fours are detestable to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 21, 'But among the winged insects that walk on all fours you may eat those that have jointed legs above their feet, with which to leap on the ground.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 22, 'Of them you may eat: the locust according to its kind, the bald locust according to its kind, the cricket according to its kind, and the grasshopper according to its kind.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 23, 'But all other winged insects that have four feet are detestable to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 24, 'By these you shall become unclean; whoever touches the carcass of any of them shall be unclean until the evening,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Unclean Animals'),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 25, 'and whoever carries any part of the carcass of any of them shall wash his clothes and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 26, 'Every animal that has divided hoofs but is not cleft-footed or does not chew the cud is unclean for you; everyone who touches one of them shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 27, 'All that walk on their paws, among the animals that walk on all fours, are unclean for you; whoever touches the carcass of any of them shall be unclean until the evening,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 28, 'and the one who carries the carcass shall wash his clothes and be unclean until the evening; they are unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 29, 'These are unclean for you among the creatures that swarm upon the earth: the weasel, the mouse, the great lizard according to its kind,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 30, 'the gecko, the land crocodile, the lizard, the sand lizard, and the chameleon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 31, 'These are unclean for you among all that swarm; whoever touches one of them when they are dead shall be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 32, 'And anything upon which any of them falls when they are dead shall be unclean, whether an article of wood or cloth or skin or sacking, any article that is used for any purpose; it shall be dipped into water, and it shall be unclean until the evening, and then it shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 33, 'And if any of them falls into any earthen vessel, all that is in it shall be unclean, and you shall break the vessel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 34, 'Any food that could be eaten shall be unclean if water from any such vessel comes upon it; and any liquid that could be drunk shall be unclean if it was in any such vessel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 35, 'Everything on which any part of the carcass falls shall be unclean; whether an oven or stove, it shall be broken in pieces; they are unclean, and shall remain unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 36, 'But a spring or a cistern holding water shall be clean, while whatever touches the carcass in it shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 37, 'If any part of their carcass falls upon any seed set aside for sowing, it is clean;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 38, 'but if water is put on the seed and any part of their carcass falls on it, it is unclean for you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 39, 'If an animal of which you may eat dies, anyone who touches its carcass shall be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 40, 'Those who eat of its carcass shall wash their clothes and be unclean until the evening; and those who carry the carcass shall wash their clothes and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 41, 'All creatures that swarm upon the earth are detestable; they shall not be eaten.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 42, 'Whatever moves on its belly, and whatever moves on all fours, or whatever has many feet, all the creatures that swarm upon the earth, you shall not eat; for they are detestable.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 43, 'You shall not make yourselves detestable with any creature that swarms; you shall not defile yourselves with them, and so become unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 44, 'For I am the LORD your God; sanctify yourselves therefore, and be holy, for I am holy. You shall not defile yourselves with any swarming creature that moves on the earth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 45, 'For I am the LORD who brought you up from the land of Egypt, to be your God; you shall be holy, for I am holy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 46, 'This is the law pertaining to land animal and bird and every living creature that moves through the waters and every creature that swarms upon the earth,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 11, 47, 'to make a distinction between the unclean and the clean, and between the living creature that may be eaten and the living creature that may not be eaten.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

If a woman conceives and bears a male child, she shall be ceremonially unclean seven days; as at the time of her menstruation, she shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 12, 3, 'On the eighth day the flesh of his foreskin shall be circumcised.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 12, 4, 'Her time of blood purification shall be thirty-three days; she shall not touch any holy thing, or come into the sanctuary, until the days of her purification are completed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 12, 5, 'If she bears a female child, she shall be unclean two weeks, as in her menstruation; her time of blood purification shall be sixty-six days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 12, 6, 'When the days of her purification are completed, whether for a son or for a daughter, she shall bring to the priest at the entrance of the tent of meeting a lamb in its first year for a burnt offering, and a pigeon or a turtledove for a sin offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 12, 7, 'He shall offer it before the LORD, and make atonement on her behalf; then she shall be clean from her flow of blood. This is the law for her who bears a child, male or female.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 12, 8, 'If she cannot afford a sheep, she shall take two turtledoves or two pigeons, one for a burnt offering and the other for a sin offering; and the priest shall make atonement on her behalf, and she shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


He shall be brought to the priest;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 3, 'the priest shall go out of the camp, and the priest shall make an examination. If the disease is healed in the leprous person,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 4, 'the priest shall command that two living clean birds and cedarwood and crimson yarn and hyssop be brought for the one who is to be cleansed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 5, 'The priest shall command that one of the birds be slaughtered over fresh water in an earthen vessel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 6, 'He shall take the living bird with the cedarwood and the crimson yarn and the hyssop, and dip them and the living bird in the blood of the bird that was slaughtered over the fresh water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 7, 'He shall sprinkle it seven times upon the one who is to be cleansed of the leprous disease; then he shall pronounce him clean, and he shall let the living bird go into the open field.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 8, 'The one who is to be cleansed shall wash his clothes, and shave off all his hair, and bathe himself in water, and he shall be clean. After that he shall come into the camp, but shall live outside his tent seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 9, 'On the seventh day he shall shave all his hair: of head, beard, eyebrows; he shall shave all his hair. Then he shall wash his clothes, and bathe his body in water, and he shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 10, 'On the eighth day he shall take two male lambs without blemish, and one ewe lamb in its first year without blemish, and a grain offering of three-tenths of an ephah of choice flour mixed with oil, and one log of oil.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 11, 'The priest who cleanses shall set the person to be cleansed, along with these things, before the LORD, at the entrance of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 12, 'The priest shall take one of the lambs, and offer it as a guilt offering, along with the log of oil, and raise them as an elevation offering before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 13, 'He shall slaughter the lamb in the place where the sin offering and the burnt offering are slaughtered in the holy place; for the guilt offering, like the sin offering, belongs to the priest: it is most holy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 14, 'The priest shall take some of the blood of the guilt offering and put it on the lobe of the right ear of the one to be cleansed, and on the thumb of the right hand, and on the big toe of the right foot.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 15, 'The priest shall take some of the log of oil and pour it into the palm of his own left hand,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 16, 'and dip his right finger in the oil that is in his left hand and sprinkle some oil with his finger seven times before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 17, 'Some of the oil that remains in his hand the priest shall put on the lobe of the right ear of the one to be cleansed, and on the thumb of the right hand, and on the big toe of the right foot, on top of the blood of the guilt offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 18, 'The rest of the oil that is in the priest"s hand he shall put on the head of the one to be cleansed. Then the priest shall make atonement on his behalf before the LORD:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 19, 'the priest shall offer the sin offering, to make atonement for the one to be cleansed from his uncleanness. Afterward he shall slaughter the burnt offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 20, 'and the priest shall offer the burnt offering and the grain offering on the altar. Thus the priest shall make atonement on his behalf and he shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 21, 'But if he is poor and cannot afford so much, he shall take one male lamb for a guilt offering to be elevated, to make atonement on his behalf, and one-tenth of an ephah of choice flour mixed with oil for a grain offering and a log of oil;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 22, 'also two turtledoves or two pigeons, such as he can afford, one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 23, 'On the eighth day he shall bring them for his cleansing to the priest, to the entrance of the tent of meeting, before the LORD;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 24, 'and the priest shall take the lamb of the guilt offering and the log of oil, and the priest shall raise them as an elevation offering before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 25, 'The priest shall slaughter the lamb of the guilt offering and shall take some of the blood of the guilt offering, and put it on the lobe of the right ear of the one to be cleansed, and on the thumb of the right hand, and on the big toe of the right foot.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 26, 'The priest shall pour some of the oil into the palm of his own left hand,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 27, 'and shall sprinkle with his right finger some of the oil that is in his left hand seven times before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 28, 'The priest shall put some of the oil that is in his hand on the lobe of the right ear of the one to be cleansed, and on the thumb of the right hand, and the big toe of the right foot, where the blood of the guilt offering was placed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 29, 'The rest of the oil that is in the priest"s hand he shall put on the head of the one to be cleansed, to make atonement on his behalf before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 30, 'And he shall offer, of the turtledoves or pigeons such as he can afford,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 31, 'one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering, along with a grain offering; and the priest shall make atonement before the LORD on behalf of the one being cleansed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 32, 'This is the ritual for the one who has a leprous disease, who cannot afford the offerings for his cleansing.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 33, 'The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 34, 'When you come into the land of Canaan, which I give you for a possession, and I put a leprous disease in a house in the land of your possession,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 35, 'the owner of the house shall come and tell the priest, saying, "There seems to me to be some sort of disease in my house."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 36, 'The priest shall command that they empty the house before the priest goes to examine the disease, or all that is in the house will become unclean; and afterward the priest shall go in to inspect the house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 37, 'He shall examine the disease; if the disease is in the walls of the house with greenish or reddish spots, and if it appears to be deeper than the surface,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 38, 'the priest shall go outside to the door of the house and shut up the house seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 39, 'The priest shall come again on the seventh day and make an inspection; if the disease has spread in the walls of the house,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 40, 'the priest shall command that the stones in which the disease appears be taken out and thrown into an unclean place outside the city.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 41, 'He shall have the inside of the house scraped thoroughly, and the plaster that is scraped off shall be dumped in an unclean place outside the city.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 42, 'They shall take other stones and put them in the place of those stones, and take other plaster and plaster the house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 43, 'If the disease breaks out again in the house, after he has taken out the stones and scraped the house and plastered it,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 44, 'the priest shall go and make inspection; if the disease has spread in the house, it is a spreading leprous disease in the house; it is unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 45, 'He shall have the house torn down, its stones and timber and all the plaster of the house, and taken outside the city to an unclean place.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 46, 'All who enter the house while it is shut up shall be unclean until the evening;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 47, 'and all who sleep in the house shall wash their clothes; and all who eat in the house shall wash their clothes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 48, 'If the priest comes and makes an inspection, and the disease has not spread in the house after the house was plastered, the priest shall pronounce the house clean; the disease is healed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 49, 'For the cleansing of the house he shall take two birds, with cedarwood and crimson yarn and hyssop,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 50, 'and shall slaughter one of the birds over fresh water in an earthen vessel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 51, 'and shall take the cedarwood and the hyssop and the crimson yarn, along with the living bird, and dip them in the blood of the slaughtered bird and the fresh water, and sprinkle the house seven times.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 52, 'Thus he shall cleanse the house with the blood of the bird, and with the fresh water, and with the living bird, and with the cedarwood and hyssop and crimson yarn;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 53, 'and he shall let the living bird go out of the city into the open field; so he shall make atonement for the house, and it shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 54, 'This is the ritual for any leprous disease: for an itch,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 55, 'for leprous diseases in clothing and houses,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 56, 'and for a swelling or an eruption or a spot,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 14, 57, 'to determine when it is unclean and when it is clean. This is the ritual for leprous diseases.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

When any man has a discharge from his member, his discharge makes him ceremonially unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 3, 'The uncleanness of his discharge is this: whether his member flows with his discharge, or his member is stopped from discharging, it is uncleanness for him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 4, 'Every bed on which the one with the discharge lies shall be unclean; and everything on which he sits shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 5, 'Anyone who touches his bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 6, 'All who sit on anything on which the one with the discharge has sat shall wash their clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 7, 'All who touch the body of the one with the discharge shall wash their clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 8, 'If the one with the discharge spits on persons who are clean, then they shall wash their clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 9, 'Any saddle on which the one with the discharge rides shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 10, 'All who touch anything that was under him shall be unclean until the evening, and all who carry such a thing shall wash their clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 11, 'All those whom the one with the discharge touches without his having rinsed his hands in water shall wash their clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 12, 'Any earthen vessel that the one with the discharge touches shall be broken; and every vessel of wood shall be rinsed in water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 13, 'When the one with a discharge is cleansed of his discharge, he shall count seven days for his cleansing; he shall wash his clothes and bathe his body in fresh water, and he shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 14, 'On the eighth day he shall take two turtledoves or two pigeons and come before the LORD to the entrance of the tent of meeting and give them to the priest.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 15, 'The priest shall offer them, one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering; and the priest shall make atonement on his behalf before the LORD for his discharge.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 16, 'If a man has an emission of semen, he shall bathe his whole body in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 17, 'Everything made of cloth or of skin on which the semen falls shall be washed with water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 18, 'If a man lies with a woman and has an emission of semen, both of them shall bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 19, 'When a woman has a discharge of blood that is her regular discharge from her body, she shall be in her impurity for seven days, and whoever touches her shall be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 20, 'Everything upon which she lies during her impurity shall be unclean; everything also upon which she sits shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 21, 'Whoever touches her bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 22, 'Whoever touches anything upon which she sits shall wash his clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 23, 'whether it is the bed or anything upon which she sits, when he touches it he shall be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 24, 'If any man lies with her, and her impurity falls on him, he shall be unclean seven days; and every bed on which he lies shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 25, 'If a woman has a discharge of blood for many days, not at the time of her impurity, or if she has a discharge beyond the time of her impurity, all the days of the discharge she shall continue in uncleanness; as in the days of her impurity, she shall be unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 26, 'Every bed on which she lies during all the days of her discharge shall be treated as the bed of her impurity; and everything on which she sits shall be unclean, as in the uncleanness of her impurity.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 27, 'Whoever touches these things shall be unclean, and shall wash his clothes, and bathe in water, and be unclean until the evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 28, 'If she is cleansed of her discharge, she shall count seven days, and after that she shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 29, 'On the eighth day she shall take two turtledoves or two pigeons and bring them to the priest at the entrance of the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 30, 'The priest shall offer one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering; and the priest shall make atonement on her behalf before the LORD for her unclean discharge.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 31, 'Thus you shall keep the people of Israel separate from their uncleanness, so that they do not die in their uncleanness by defiling my tabernacle that is in their midst.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 32, 'This is the ritual for those who have a discharge: for him who has an emission of semen, becoming unclean thereby,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 15, 33, 'for her who is in the infirmity of her period, for anyone, male or female, who has a discharge, and for the man who lies with a woman who is unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

Tell your brother Aaron not to come just at any time into the sanctuary inside the curtain before the mercy seat that is upon the ark, or he will die; for I appear in the cloud upon the mercy seat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 3, 'Thus shall Aaron come into the holy place: with a young bull for a sin offering and a ram for a burnt offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 4, 'He shall put on the holy linen tunic, and shall have the linen undergarments next to his body, fasten the linen sash, and wear the linen turban; these are the holy vestments. He shall bathe his body in water, and then put them on.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 5, 'He shall take from the congregation of the people of Israel two male goats for a sin offering, and one ram for a burnt offering.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 6, 'Aaron shall offer the bull as a sin offering for himself, and shall make atonement for himself and for his house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 7, 'He shall take the two goats and set them before the LORD at the entrance of the tent of meeting;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 8, 'and Aaron shall cast lots on the two goats, one lot for the LORD and the other lot for Azazel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 9, 'Aaron shall present the goat on which the lot fell for the LORD, and offer it as a sin offering;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 10, 'but the goat on which the lot fell for Azazel shall be presented alive before the LORD to make atonement over it, that it may be sent away into the wilderness to Azazel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 11, 'Aaron shall present the bull as a sin offering for himself, and shall make atonement for himself and for his house; he shall slaughter the bull as a sin offering for himself.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 12, 'He shall take a censer full of coals of fire from the altar before the LORD, and two handfuls of crushed sweet incense, and he shall bring it inside the curtain', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 13, 'and put the incense on the fire before the LORD, that the cloud of the incense may cover the mercy seat that is upon the covenant, or he will die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 14, 'He shall take some of the blood of the bull, and sprinkle it with his finger on the front of the mercy seat, and before the mercy seat he shall sprinkle the blood with his finger seven times.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 15, 'He shall slaughter the goat of the sin offering that is for the people and bring its blood inside the curtain, and do with its blood as he did with the blood of the bull, sprinkling it upon the mercy seat and before the mercy seat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 16, 'Thus he shall make atonement for the sanctuary, because of the uncleannesses of the people of Israel, and because of their transgressions, all their sins; and so he shall do for the tent of meeting, which remains with them in the midst of their uncleannesses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 17, 'No one shall be in the tent of meeting from the time he enters to make atonement in the sanctuary until he comes out and has made atonement for himself and for his house and for all the assembly of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 18, 'Then he shall go out to the altar that is before the LORD and make atonement on its behalf, and shall take some of the blood of the bull and of the blood of the goat, and put it on each of the horns of the altar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 19, 'He shall sprinkle some of the blood on it with his finger seven times, and cleanse it and hallow it from the uncleannesses of the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 20, 'When he has finished atoning for the holy place and the tent of meeting and the altar, he shall present the live goat.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 21, 'Then Aaron shall lay both his hands on the head of the live goat, and confess over it all the iniquities of the people of Israel, and all their transgressions, all their sins, putting them on the head of the goat, and sending it away into the wilderness by means of someone designated for the task.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 22, 'The goat shall bear on itself all their iniquities to a barren region; and the goat shall be set free in the wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 23, 'Then Aaron shall enter the tent of meeting, and shall take off the linen vestments that he put on when he went into the holy place, and shall leave them there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 24, 'He shall bathe his body in water in a holy place, and put on his vestments; then he shall come out and offer his burnt offering and the burnt offering of the people, making atonement for himself and for the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 25, 'The fat of the sin offering he shall turn into smoke on the altar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 26, 'The one who sets the goat free for Azazel shall wash his clothes and bathe his body in water, and afterward may come into the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 27, 'The bull of the sin offering and the goat of the sin offering, whose blood was brought in to make atonement in the holy place, shall be taken outside the camp; their skin and their flesh and their dung shall be consumed in fire.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 28, 'The one who burns them shall wash his clothes and bathe his body in water, and afterward may come into the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 29, 'This shall be a statute to you forever: In the seventh month, on the tenth day of the month, you shall deny yourselves, and shall do no work, neither the citizen nor the alien who resides among you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 30, 'For on this day atonement shall be made for you, to cleanse you; from all your sins you shall be clean before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 31, 'It is a sabbath of complete rest to you, and you shall deny yourselves; it is a statute forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 32, 'The priest who is anointed and consecrated as priest in his father"s place shall make atonement, wearing the linen vestments, the holy vestments.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 33, 'He shall make atonement for the sanctuary, and he shall make atonement for the tent of meeting and for the altar, and he shall make atonement for the priests and for all the people of the assembly.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 16, 34, 'This shall be an everlasting statute for you, to make atonement for the people of Israel once in the year for all their sins. And Moses did as the LORD had commanded him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);




Any of the people of Israel, or of the aliens who reside in Israel, who give any of their offspring to Molech shall be put to death; the people of the land shall stone them to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 3, 'I myself will set my face against them, and will cut them off from the people, because they have given of their offspring to Molech, defiling my sanctuary and profaning my holy name.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 4, 'And if the people of the land should ever close their eyes to them, when they give of their offspring to Molech, and do not put them to death,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 5, 'I myself will set my face against them and against their family, and will cut them off from among their people, them and all who follow them in prostituting themselves to Molech.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 6, 'If any turn to mediums and wizards, prostituting themselves to them, I will set my face against them, and will cut them off from the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 7, 'Consecrate yourselves therefore, and be holy; for I am the LORD your God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 8, 'Keep my statutes, and observe them; I am the LORD; I sanctify you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 9, 'All who curse father or mother shall be put to death; having cursed father or mother, their blood is upon them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 10, 'If a man commits adultery with the wife of his neighbor, both the adulterer and the adulteress shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 11, 'The man who lies with his father"s wife has uncovered his father"s nakedness; both of them shall be put to death; their blood is upon them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 12, 'If a man lies with his daughter-in-law, both of them shall be put to death; they have committed perversion, their blood is upon them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 13, 'If a man lies with a male as with a woman, both of them have committed an abomination; they shall be put to death; their blood is upon them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 14, 'If a man takes a wife and her mother also, it is depravity; they shall be burned to death, both he and they, that there may be no depravity among you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 15, 'If a man has sexual relations with an animal, he shall be put to death; and you shall kill the animal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 16, 'If a woman approaches any animal and has sexual relations with it, you shall kill the woman and the animal; they shall be put to death, their blood is upon them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 17, 'If a man takes his sister, a daughter of his father or a daughter of his mother, and sees her nakedness, and she sees his nakedness, it is a disgrace, and they shall be cut off in the sight of their people; he has uncovered his sister"s nakedness, he shall be subject to punishment.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 18, 'If a man lies with a woman having her sickness and uncovers her nakedness, he has laid bare her flow and she has laid bare her flow of blood; both of them shall be cut off from their people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 19, 'You shall not uncover the nakedness of your mother"s sister or of your father"s sister, for that is to lay bare one"s own flesh; they shall be subject to punishment.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 20, 'If a man lies with his uncle"s wife, he has uncovered his uncle"s nakedness; they shall be subject to punishment; they shall die childless.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 21, 'If a man takes his brother"s wife, it is impurity; he has uncovered his brother"s nakedness; they shall be childless.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 22, 'You shall keep all my statutes and all my ordinances, and observe them, so that the land to which I bring you to settle in may not vomit you out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 23, 'You shall not follow the practices of the nation that I am driving out before you. Because they did all these things, I abhorred them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 24, 'But I have said to you: You shall inherit their land, and I will give it to you to possess, a land flowing with milk and honey. I am the LORD your God; I have separated you from the peoples.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 25, 'You shall therefore make a distinction between the clean animal and the unclean, and between the unclean bird and the clean; you shall not bring abomination on yourselves by animal or by bird or by anything with which the ground teems, which I have set apart for you to hold unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 26, 'You shall be holy to me; for I the LORD am holy, and I have separated you from the other peoples to be mine.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 20, 27, 'A man or a woman who is a medium or a wizard shall be put to death; they shall be stoned to death, their blood is upon them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

No one shall defile himself for a dead person among his relatives,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Holiness of Priests'),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 2, 'except for his nearest kin: his mother, his father, his son, his daughter, his brother;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 3, 'likewise, for a virgin sister, close to him because she has had no husband, he may defile himself for her.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 4, 'But he shall not defile himself as a husband among his people and so profane himself.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 5, 'They shall not make bald spots upon their heads, or shave off the edges of their beards, or make any gashes in their flesh.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 6, 'They shall be holy to their God, and not profane the name of their God; for they offer the LORD"s offerings by fire, the food of their God; therefore they shall be holy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 7, 'They shall not marry a prostitute or a woman who has been defiled; neither shall they marry a woman divorced from her husband. For they are holy to their God,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 8, 'and you shall treat them as holy, since they offer the food of your God; they shall be holy to you, for I the LORD, I who sanctify you, am holy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 9, 'When the daughter of a priest profanes herself through prostitution, she profanes her father; she shall be burned to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 10, 'The priest who is exalted above his fellows, on whose head the anointing oil has been poured and who has been consecrated to wear the vestments, shall not dishevel his hair, nor tear his vestments.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 11, 'He shall not go where there is a dead body; he shall not defile himself even for his father or mother.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 12, 'He shall not go outside the sanctuary and thus profane the sanctuary of his God; for the consecration of the anointing oil of his God is upon him: I am the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 13, 'He shall marry only a woman who is a virgin.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 14, 'A widow, or a divorced woman, or a woman who has been defiled, a prostitute, these he shall not marry. He shall marry a virgin of his own kin,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 15, 'that he may not profane his offspring among his kin; for I am the LORD; I sanctify him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 16, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 17, 'Speak to Aaron and say: No one of your offspring throughout their generations who has a blemish may approach to offer the food of his God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 18, 'For no one who has a blemish shall draw near, one who is blind or lame, or one who has a mutilated face or a limb too long,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 19, 'or one who has a broken foot or a broken hand,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 20, 'or a hunchback, or a dwarf, or a man with a blemish in his eyes or an itching disease or scabs or crushed testicles.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 21, 'No descendant of Aaron the priest who has a blemish shall come near to offer the LORD"s offerings by fire; since he has a blemish, he shall not come near to offer the food of his God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 22, 'He may eat the food of his God, of the most holy as well as of the holy.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 23, 'But he shall not come near the curtain or approach the altar, because he has a blemish, that he may not profane my sanctuaries; for I am the LORD; I sanctify them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(3, 'Ima', 'Leviticus', 21, 24, 'Thus Moses spoke to Aaron and to his sons and to all the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);







From Reuben, Elizur son of Shedeur.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 6, 'From Simeon, Shelumiel son of Zurishaddai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 7, 'From Judah, Nahshon son of Amminadab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 8, 'From Issachar, Nethanel son of Zuar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 9, 'From Zebulun, Eliab son of Helon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 10, 'From the sons of Joseph:  
from Ephraim, Elishama son of Ammihud;  
from Manasseh, Gamaliel son of Pedahzur.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 11, 'From Benjamin, Abidan son of Gideoni.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 12, 'From Dan, Ahiezer son of Ammishaddai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 13, 'From Asher, Pagiel son of Ochran.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 14, 'From Gad, Eliasaph son of Deuel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 15, 'From Naphtali, Ahira son of Enan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 16, 'These were the ones chosen from the congregation, the leaders of their ancestral tribes, the heads of the divisions of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 17, 'Moses and Aaron took these men who had been designated by name,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 18, 'and on the first day of the second month they assembled the whole congregation together. They registered themselves in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names from twenty years old and upward, individually,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 19, 'as the LORD commanded Moses. So he enrolled them in the wilderness of Sinai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 20, 'The descendants of Reuben, Israel"s firstborn, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, individually, every male from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 21, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Reuben were forty-six thousand five hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 22, 'The descendants of Simeon, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, those of them that were numbered, according to the number of names, individually, every male from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 23, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Simeon were fifty-nine thousand three hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 24, 'The descendants of Gad, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 25, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Gad were forty-five thousand six hundred fifty.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 26, 'The descendants of Judah, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 27, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Judah were seventy-four thousand six hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 28, 'The descendants of Issachar, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 29, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Issachar were fifty-four thousand four hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 30, 'The descendants of Zebulun, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 31, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Zebulun were fifty-seven thousand four hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 32, 'The descendants of Joseph, namely, the descendants of Ephraim, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 33, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Ephraim were forty thousand five hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 34, 'The descendants of Manasseh, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 35, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Manasseh were thirty-two thousand two hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 36, 'The descendants of Benjamin, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 37, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Benjamin were thirty-five thousand four hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 38, 'The descendants of Dan, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 39, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Dan were sixty-two thousand seven hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 40, 'The descendants of Asher, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 41, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Asher were forty-one thousand five hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 42, 'The descendants of Naphtali, their lineage, in their clans, by their ancestral houses, according to the number of names, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 43, 'those enrolled of the tribe of Naphtali were fifty-three thousand four hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 44, 'These are those who were enrolled, whom Moses and Aaron enrolled with the help of the leaders of Israel, twelve men, each representing his ancestral house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 45, 'So the whole number of the Israelites, by their ancestral houses, from twenty years old and upward, everyone able to go to war in Israel--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 46, 'their whole number was six hundred three thousand five hundred fifty.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 47, 'The Levites, however, were not numbered by their ancestral tribe along with them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 48, 'The LORD had said to Moses:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 49, 'Only the tribe of Levi you shall not enroll, and you shall not take a census of them with the other Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 50, 'Rather you shall appoint the Levites over the tabernacle of the covenant, and over all its equipment, and over all that belongs to it; they are to carry the tabernacle and all its equipment, and they shall tend it, and shall camp around the tabernacle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 51, 'When the tabernacle is to set out, the Levites shall take it down; and when the tabernacle is to be pitched, the Levites shall set it up. And any outsider who comes near shall be put to death.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 52, 'The other Israelites shall camp in their respective regimental camps, by companies;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 53, 'but the Levites shall camp around the tabernacle of the covenant, that there may be no wrath on the congregation of the Israelites; and the Levites shall perform the guard duty of the tabernacle of the covenant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 1, 54, 'The Israelites did so; they did just as the LORD commanded Moses.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);









"Arise, O LORD, let your enemies be scattered,  
    and your foes flee before you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 10, 36, 'And whenever it came to rest, he would say,
"Return, O LORD of the ten thousand thousands of Israel."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


When there are prophets among you,  
    I the LORD make myself known to them in visions;  
    I speak to them in dreams.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 7, 'Not so with my servant Moses;  
    he is entrusted with all my house.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 8, 'With him I speak face to face-- clearly, not in riddles;  
    and he beholds the form of the LORD.
Why then were you not afraid to speak against my servant Moses?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 9, 'And the anger of the LORD was kindled against them, and he departed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 10, 'When the cloud went away from over the tent, Miriam had become leprous, as white as snow. And Aaron turned towards Miriam and saw that she was leprous.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 11, 'Then Aaron said to Moses, "Oh, my lord, do not punish us for a sin that we have so foolishly committed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 12, 'Do not let her be like one stillborn, whose flesh is half consumed when it comes out of its mother"s womb."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 13, 'And Moses cried to the LORD, "O God, please heal her."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 14, 'But the LORD said to Moses, "If her father had but spit in her face, would she not bear her shame for seven days? Let her be shut out of the camp for seven days, and after that she may be brought in again."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 15, 'So Miriam was shut out of the camp for seven days; and the people did not set out on the march until Miriam had been brought in again.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 12, 16, 'After that the people set out from Hazeroth, and camped in the wilderness of Paran.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


Then the glory of the LORD appeared at the tent of meeting to all the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 11, 'And the LORD said to Moses, "How long will this people despise me? And how long will they refuse to believe in me, in spite of all the signs that I have done among them?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 12, 'I will strike them with pestilence and disinherit them, and I will make of you a nation greater and mightier than they."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 13, 'But Moses said to the LORD, "Then the Egyptians will hear of it, for in your might you brought up this people from among them,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Moses Intercedes for the People'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 14, 'and they will tell the inhabitants of this land. They have heard that you, O LORD, are in the midst of this people; for you, O LORD, are seen face to face, and your cloud stands over them and you go in front of them, in a pillar of cloud by day and in a pillar of fire by night.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 15, 'Now if you kill this people all at one time, then the nations who have heard about you will say,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 16, '"It is because the LORD was not able to bring this people into the land he swore to give them that he has slaughtered them in the wilderness."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 17, 'And now, therefore, let the power of the LORD be great in the way that you promised when you spoke, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 18, '"The LORD is slow to anger,  
and abounding in steadfast love,  
forgiving iniquity and transgression,  
but by no means clearing the guilty,  
visiting the iniquity of the parents  
upon the children  
to the third and the fourth generation."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 19, 'Forgive the iniquity of this people according to the greatness of your steadfast love, just as you have pardoned this people, from Egypt even until now."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 20, 'Then the LORD said, "I do forgive, just as you have asked;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 21, 'nevertheless--as I live, and as all the earth shall be filled with the glory of the LORD--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 22, 'none of the people who have seen my glory and the signs that I did in Egypt and in the wilderness, and yet have tested me these ten times and have not obeyed my voice,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 23, 'shall see the land that I swore to give to their ancestors; none of those who despised me shall see it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 24, 'But my servant Caleb, because he has a different spirit and has followed me wholeheartedly, I will bring into the land into which he went, and his descendants shall possess it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 25, 'Now, since the Amalekites and the Canaanites live in the valleys, turn tomorrow and set out for the wilderness by the way to the Red Sea."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 26, 'And the LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'An Attempted Invasion is Repulsed'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 27, 'How long shall this wicked congregation complain against me? I have heard the complaints of the Israelites, which they complain against me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 28, 'Say to them, "As I live," says the LORD, "I will do to you the very things I heard you say:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 29, 'your dead bodies shall fall in this very wilderness; and of all your number, included in the census, from twenty years old and upward, who have complained against me,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 30, 'not one of you shall come into the land in which I swore to settle you, except Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 31, 'But your little ones, who you said would become booty, I will bring in, and they shall know the land that you have despised.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 32, 'But as for you, your dead bodies shall fall in this wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 33, 'And your children shall be shepherds in the wilderness for forty years, and shall suffer for your faithlessness, until the last of your dead bodies lies in the wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 34, 'According to the number of the days in which you spied out the land, forty days, for every day a year, you shall bear your iniquity, forty years, and you shall know my displeasure."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 35, 'I the LORD have spoken; surely I will do thus to all this wicked congregation gathered together against me: in this wilderness they shall come to a full end, and there they shall die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 36, 'And the men whom Moses sent to spy out the land, who returned and made all the congregation complain against him by bringing a bad report about the land--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 37, 'the men who brought an unfavorable report about the land died by a plague before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 38, 'But Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh alone remained alive, of those men who went to spy out the land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 39, 'When Moses told these words to all the Israelites, the people mourned greatly.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 40, 'They rose early in the morning and went up to the heights of the hill country, saying, "Here we are. We will go up to the place that the LORD has promised, for we have sinned."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 41, 'But Moses said, "Why do you continue to transgress the command of the LORD? That will not succeed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 42, 'Do not go up, for the LORD is not with you; do not let yourselves be struck down before your enemies.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 43, 'For the Amalekites and the Canaanites will confront you there, and you shall fall by the sword; because you have turned back from following the LORD, the LORD will not be with you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 44, 'But they presumed to go up to the heights of the hill country, even though the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and Moses, had not left the camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 14, 45, 'Then the Amalekites and the Canaanites who lived in that hill country came down and defeated them, pursuing them as far as Hormah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);





This shall be a perpetual statute for the Israelites and for the alien residing among them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 11, 'Those who touch the dead body of any human being shall be unclean seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 12, 'They shall purify themselves with the water on the third day and on the seventh day, and so be clean; but if they do not purify themselves on the third day and on the seventh day, they will not become clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 13, 'All who touch a corpse, the body of a human being who has died, and do not purify themselves, defile the tabernacle of the LORD; such persons shall be cut off from Israel. Since water for cleansing was not dashed on them, they remain unclean; their uncleanness is still on them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 14, 'This is the law when someone dies in a tent: everyone who comes into the tent, and everyone who is in the tent, shall be unclean seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 15, 'And every open vessel with no cover fastened on it is unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 16, 'Whoever in the open field touches one who has been killed by a sword, or who has died naturally, or a human bone, or a grave, shall be unclean seven days.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 17, 'For the unclean they shall take some ashes of the burnt purification offering, and running water shall be added in a vessel;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 18, 'then a clean person shall take hyssop, dip it in the water, and sprinkle it on the tent, on all the furnishings, on the persons who were there, and on whoever touched the bone, the slain, the corpse, or the grave.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 19, 'The clean person shall sprinkle the unclean ones on the third day and on the seventh day, thus purifying them on the seventh day. Then they shall wash their clothes and bathe themselves in water, and at evening they shall be clean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 20, 'Any who are unclean but do not purify themselves, those persons shall be cut off from the assembly, for they have defiled the sanctuary of the LORD. Since the water for cleansing has not been dashed on them, they are unclean.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 21, 'It shall be a perpetual statute for them. The one who sprinkles the water for cleansing shall wash his clothes, and whoever touches the water for cleansing shall be unclean until evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 19, 22, 'Whatever the unclean person touches shall be unclean, and anyone who touches it shall be unclean until evening.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


"Waheb in Suphah and the wadis.  
The Arnon', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 15, 'and the slopes of the wadis  
that extend to the seat of Ar,  
and lie along the border of Moab."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 16, 'From there they continued to Beer; that is the well of which the LORD said to Moses, "Gather the people together, and I will give them water."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 17, 'Then Israel sang this song:
"Spring up, O well!--Sing to it!--', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 18, 'the well that the leaders sank,  
that the nobles of the people dug,  
with the scepter, with the staff."
From the wilderness to Mattanah,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 19, 'from Mattanah to Nahaliel, from Nahaliel to Bamoth,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 20, 'and from Bamoth to the valley lying in the region of Moab by the top of Pisgah that overlooks the wasteland.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 21, 'Then Israel sent messengers to King Sihon of the Amorites, saying,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'King Sihon Defeated'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 22, '"Let me pass through your land; we will not turn aside into field or vineyard; we will not drink the water of any well; we will go by the King"s Highway until we have passed through your territory."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 23, 'But Sihon would not allow Israel to pass through his territory. Sihon gathered all his people together, and went out against Israel to the wilderness; he came to Jahaz, and fought against Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 24, 'Israel put him to the sword, and took possession of his land from the Arnon to the Jabbok, as far as to the Ammonites; for the boundary of the Ammonites was strong.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 25, 'Israel took all these towns, and Israel settled in all the towns of the Amorites, in Heshbon, and in all its villages.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 26, 'For Heshbon was the city of King Sihon of the Amorites, who had fought against the former king of Moab and captured all his land as far as the Arnon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 27, 'Therefore the ballad singers say,
"Come to Heshbon, let it be built;  
    let the city of Sihon be established.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 28, 'For fire came out from Heshbon,  
    flame from the city of Sihon.  
It devoured Ar of Moab,  
    and swallowed up the heights of the Arnon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 29, 'Woe to you, O Moab!  
    You are undone, O people of Chemosh!  
He has made his sons fugitives,  
    and his daughters captives,  
    to an Amorite king, Sihon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 30, 'So their posterity perished  
    from Heshbon to Dibon,  
    and we laid waste until fire spread to Medeba."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 31, 'Thus Israel settled in the land of the Amorites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 32, 'Moses sent to spy out Jazer; and they captured its villages, and dispossessed the Amorites who were there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 33, 'Then they turned and went up the road to Bashan; and King Og of Bashan came out against them, he and all his people, to battle at Edrei.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'King Og Defeated'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 34, 'But the LORD said to Moses, "Do not be afraid of him; for I have given him into your hand, with all his people, and all his land. You shall do to him as you did to King Sihon of the Amorites, who ruled in Heshbon."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 21, 35, 'So they killed him, his sons, and all his people, until there was no survivor left; and they took possession of his land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


"Balak has brought me from Aram,  
    the king of Moab from the eastern mountains:  
"Come, curse Jacob for me;  
    Come, denounce Israel!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 8, 'How can I curse whom God has not cursed?  
    How can I denounce those whom the LORD has not denounced?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 9, 'For from the top of the crags I see him,  
    from the hills I behold him.  
Here is a people living alone,  
    and not reckoning itself among the nations!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 10, 'Who can count the dust of Jacob,  
    or number the dust-cloud of Israel?  
Let me die the death of the upright,  
    and let my end be like his!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 11, 'Then Balak said to Balaam, "What have you done to me? I brought you to curse my enemies, but now you have done nothing but bless them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 12, 'He answered, "Must I not take care to say what the LORD puts into my mouth?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 13, 'So Balak said to him, "Come with me to another place from which you may see them; you shall see only part of them, and shall not see them all; then curse them for me from there."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Balaam"s Second Oracle'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 14, 'So he took him to the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah. He built seven altars, and offered a bull and a ram on each altar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 15, 'Balaam said to Balak, "Stand here beside your burnt offerings, while I meet the LORD over there."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 16, 'The LORD met Balaam, put a word into his mouth, and said, "Return to Balak, and this is what you shall say."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 17, 'When he came to him, he was standing beside his burnt offerings with the officials of Moab. Balak said to him, "What has the LORD said?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 18, 'Then Balaam uttered his oracle, saying:
"Rise, Balak, and hear;  
    listen to me, O son of Zippor:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 19, 'God is not a human being, that he should lie,  
    or a mortal, that he should change his mind.  
Has he promised, and will he not do it?  
    Has he spoken, and will he not fulfill it?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 20, 'See, I received a command to bless;  
    he has blessed, and I cannot revoke it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 21, 'He has not beheld misfortune in Jacob;  
    nor has he seen trouble in Israel.  
The LORD their God is with them,  
    acclaimed as a king among them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 22, 'God, who brings them out of Egypt,  
    is like the horns of a wild ox for them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 23, 'Surely there is no enchantment against Jacob,  
    no divination against Israel;  
now it shall be said of Jacob and Israel,  
    "See what God has done!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 24, 'Look, a people rising up like a lioness,  
    and rousing itself like a lion!  
It does not lie down until it has eaten the prey  
    and drunk the blood of the slain."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 25, 'Then Balak said to Balaam, "Do not curse them at all, and do not bless them at all."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 26, 'But Balaam answered Balak, "Did I not tell you, "Whatever the LORD says, that is what I must do"?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 27, 'So Balak said to Balaam, "Come now, I will take you to another place; perhaps it will please God that you may curse them for me from there."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 28, 'So Balak took Balaam to the top of Peor, which overlooks the wasteland.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 29, 'Balaam said to Balak, "Build me seven altars here, and prepare seven bulls and seven rams for me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 23, 30, 'So Balak did as Balaam had said, and offered a bull and a ram on each altar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"The oracle of Balaam son of Beor,  
    the oracle of the man whose eye is clear,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 4, 'the oracle of one who hears the words of God,  
    who sees the vision of the Almighty,  
    who falls down, but with eyes uncovered:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 5, 'how fair are your tents, O Jacob,  
    your encampments, O Israel!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 6, 'Like palm groves that stretch far away,  
    like gardens beside a river,  
like aloes that the LORD has planted,  
    like cedar trees beside the waters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 7, 'Water shall flow from his buckets,  
    and his seed shall have abundant water,  
his king shall be higher than Agag,  
    and his kingdom shall be exalted.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 8, 'God who brings him out of Egypt,  
    is like the horns of a wild ox for him;  
he shall devour the nations that are his foes  
    and break their bones.  
    He shall strike with his arrows.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 9, 'He crouched, he lay down like a lion,  
    and like a lioness; who will rouse him up?  
Blessed is everyone who blesses you,  
    and cursed is everyone who curses you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 10, 'Then Balak"s anger was kindled against Balaam, and he struck his hands together. Balak said to Balaam, "I summoned you to curse my enemies, but instead you have blessed them these three times.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 11, 'Now be off with you! Go home! I said, "I will reward you richly," but the LORD has denied you any reward."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 12, 'And Balaam said to Balak, "Did I not tell your messengers whom you sent to me,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 13, '"If Balak should give me his house full of silver and gold, I would not be able to go beyond the word of the LORD, to do either good or bad of my own will; what the LORD says, that is what I will say"?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 14, 'So now, I am going to my people; let me advise you what this people will do to your people in days to come."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 15, 'So he uttered his oracle, saying:
"The oracle of Balaam son of Beor,  
    the oracle of the man whose eye is clear,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Balaam"s Fourth Oracle'),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 16, 'the oracle of one who hears the words of God,  
    and knows the knowledge of the Most High,  
who sees the vision of the Almighty,  
    who falls down, but with his eyes uncovered:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 17, 'I see him, but not now;  
    I behold him, but not near--  
a star shall come out of Jacob,  
    and a scepter shall rise out of Israel;  
it shall crush the borderlands of Moab,  
    and the territory of all the Shethites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 18, 'Edom will become a possession,  
    Seir a possession of its enemies,  
    while Israel does valiantly.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 19, 'One out of Jacob shall rule,  
    and destroy the survivors of Ir."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 20, 'Then he looked on Amalek, and uttered his oracle, saying:
"First among the nations was Amalek,  
but its end is to perish forever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 21, 'Then he looked on the Kenite, and uttered his oracle, saying:
"Enduring is your dwelling place,  
    and your nest is set in the rock;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 22, 'yet Kain is destined for burning.  
    How long shall Asshur take you away captive?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 23, 'Again he uttered his oracle, saying:
"Alas, who shall live when God does this?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 24, 'But ships shall come from Kittim  
and shall afflict Asshur and Eber;  
    and he also shall perish forever."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 24, 25, 'Then Balaam got up and went back to his place, and Balak also went his way.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


The Israelites, who came out of the land of Egypt, were:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 5, 'Reuben, the firstborn of Israel. The descendants of Reuben: of Hanoch, the clan of the Hanochites; of Pallu, the clan of the Palluites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 6, 'of Hezron, the clan of the Hezronites; of Carmi, the clan of the Carmites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 7, 'These are the clans of the Reubenites; the number of those enrolled was forty-three thousand seven hundred thirty.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 8, 'And the descendants of Pallu: Eliab.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 9, 'The descendants of Eliab: Nemuel, Dathan, and Abiram. These are the same Dathan and Abiram, chosen from the congregation, who rebelled against Moses and Aaron in the company of Korah, when they rebelled against the LORD,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 10, 'and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up along with Korah, when that company died, when the fire devoured two hundred fifty men; and they became a warning.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 11, 'Notwithstanding, the sons of Korah did not die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 12, 'The descendants of Simeon by their clans: of Nemuel, the clan of the Nemuelites; of Jamin, the clan of the Jaminites; of Jachin, the clan of the Jachinites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 13, 'of Zerah, the clan of the Zerahites; of Shaul, the clan of the Shaulites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 14, 'These are the clans of the Simeonites, twenty-two thousand two hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 15, 'The children of Gad by their clans: of Zephon, the clan of the Zephonites; of Haggi, the clan of the Haggites; of Shuni, the clan of the Shunites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 16, 'of Ozni, the clan of the Oznites; of Eri, the clan of the Erites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 17, 'of Arod, the clan of the Arodites; of Areli, the clan of the Arelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 18, 'These are the clans of the Gadites: the number of those enrolled was forty thousand five hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 19, 'The sons of Judah: Er and Onan; Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 20, 'The descendants of Judah by their clans were: of Shelah, the clan of the Shelanites; of Perez, the clan of the Perezites; of Zerah, the clan of the Zerahites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 21, 'The descendants of Perez were: of Hezron, the clan of the Hezronites; of Hamul, the clan of the Hamulites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 22, 'These are the clans of Judah: the number of those enrolled was seventy-six thousand five hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 23, 'The descendants of Issachar by their clans: of Tola, the clan of the Tolaites; of Puvah, the clan of the Punites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 24, 'of Jashub, the clan of the Jashubites; of Shimron, the clan of the Shimronites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 25, 'These are the clans of Issachar: sixty-four thousand three hundred enrolled.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 26, 'The descendants of Zebulun by their clans: of Sered, the clan of the Seredites; of Elon, the clan of the Elonites; of Jahleel, the clan of the Jahleelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 27, 'These are the clans of the Zebulunites; the number of those enrolled was sixty thousand five hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 28, 'The sons of Joseph by their clans: Manasseh and Ephraim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 29, 'The descendants of Manasseh: of Machir, the clan of the Machirites; and Machir was the father of Gilead; of Gilead, the clan of the Gileadites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 30, 'These are the descendants of Gilead: of Iezer, the clan of the Iezerites; of Helek, the clan of the Helekites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 31, 'and of Asriel, the clan of the Asrielites; and of Shechem, the clan of the Shechemites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 32, 'and of Shemida, the clan of the Shemidaites; and of Hepher, the clan of the Hepherites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 33, 'Now Zelophehad son of Hepher had no sons, but daughters: and the names of the daughters of Zelophehad were Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 34, 'These are the clans of Manasseh; the number of those enrolled was fifty-two thousand seven hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 35, 'These are the descendants of Ephraim according to their clans: of Shuthelah, the clan of the Shuthelahites; of Becher, the clan of the Becherites; of Tahan, the clan of the Tahanites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 36, 'And these are the descendants of Shuthelah: of Eran, the clan of the Eranites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 37, 'These are the clans of the Ephraimites: the number of those enrolled was thirty-two thousand five hundred. These are the descendants of Joseph by their clans.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 38, 'The descendants of Benjamin by their clans: of Bela, the clan of the Belaites; of Ashbel, the clan of the Ashbelites; of Ahiram, the clan of the Ahiramites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 39, 'of Shephupham, the clan of the Shuphamites; of Hupham, the clan of the Huphamites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 40, 'And the sons of Bela were Ard and Naaman: of Ard, the clan of the Ardites; of Naaman, the clan of the Naamites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 41, 'These are the descendants of Benjamin by their clans; the number of those enrolled was forty-five thousand six hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 42, 'These are the descendants of Dan by their clans: of Shuham, the clan of the Shuhamites. These are the clans of Dan by their clans.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 43, 'All the clans of the Shuhamites: sixty-four thousand four hundred enrolled.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 44, 'The descendants of Asher by their families: of Imnah, the clan of the Imnites; of Ishvi, the clan of the Ishvites; of Beriah, the clan of the Beriites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 45, 'Of the descendants of Beriah: of Heber, the clan of the Heberites; of Malchiel, the clan of the Malchielites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 46, 'And the name of the daughter of Asher was Serah.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 47, 'These are the clans of the Asherites: the number of those enrolled was fifty-three thousand four hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 48, 'The descendants of Naphtali by their clans: of Jahzeel, the clan of the Jahzeelites; of Guni, the clan of the Gunites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 49, 'of Jezer, the clan of the Jezerites; of Shillem, the clan of the Shillemites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 50, 'These are the Naphtalites by their clans: the number of those enrolled was forty-five thousand four hundred.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 51, 'This was the number of the Israelites enrolled: six hundred and one thousand seven hundred thirty.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 52, 'The LORD spoke to Moses, saying:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 53, 'To these the land shall be apportioned for inheritance according to the number of names.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 54, 'To a large tribe you shall give a large inheritance, and to a small tribe you shall give a small inheritance; every tribe shall be given its inheritance according to its enrollment.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 55, 'But the land shall be apportioned by lot; according to the names of their ancestral tribes they shall inherit.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 56, 'Their inheritance shall be apportioned according to lot between the larger and the smaller.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 57, 'This is the enrollment of the Levites by their clans: of Gershon, the clan of the Gershonites; of Kohath, the clan of the Kohathites; of Merari, the clan of the Merarites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 58, 'These are the clans of Levi: the clan of the Libnites, the clan of the Hebronites, the clan of the Mahlites, the clan of the Mushites, the clan of the Korahites. Now Kohath was the father of Amram.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 59, 'The name of Amram"s wife was Jochebed daughter of Levi, who was born to Levi in Egypt; and she bore to Amram: Aaron, Moses, and their sister Miriam.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 60, 'To Aaron were born Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 61, 'But Nadab and Abihu died when they offered unholy fire before the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 62, 'The number of those enrolled was twenty-three thousand, every male one month old and upward; for they were not enrolled among the Israelites because there was no allotment given to them among the Israelites.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 63, 'These were those enrolled by Moses and Eleazar the priest, who enrolled the Israelites in the plains of Moab by the Jordan opposite Jericho.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 64, 'Among these there was not one of those enrolled by Moses and Aaron the priest, who had enrolled the Israelites in the wilderness of Sinai.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(4, 'Bil', 'Numbers', 26, 65, 'For the LORD had said of them, "They shall die in the wilderness." Not one of them was left, except Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);











